1
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:10,560
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

2
00:00:10,585 --> 00:00:13,285
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

3
00:00:13,895 --> 00:00:15,695
On September 26,

4
00:00:15,695 --> 00:00:18,365
the second Last Stage: 24H was revealed.

5
00:00:19,795 --> 00:00:22,035
The four directors who lost the matchup...

6
00:00:22,035 --> 00:00:25,365
are on the Last Stage for survival.

7
00:00:25,365 --> 00:00:27,135
Only 24 hours are given...

8
00:00:27,135 --> 00:00:28,735
to four directors.

9
00:00:28,905 --> 00:00:31,175
And 20 cubes.

10
00:00:31,505 --> 00:00:32,875
(What am I supposed to do?)

11
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:33,945
(This is crazy.)

12
00:00:33,945 --> 00:00:36,175
(I can't create any choreography.)

13
00:00:36,175 --> 00:00:37,585
(Mental breakdown)

14
00:00:37,585 --> 00:00:39,345
(I was completely clueless.)

15
00:00:39,345 --> 00:00:40,345
(There was no guideline or whatsoever.)

16
00:00:40,345 --> 00:00:41,555
(I'll just go home.)

17
00:00:42,015 --> 00:00:43,585
(There's nothing I can do with these.)

18
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:47,595
They had to interpret 20 cubes in their own ways...

19
00:00:47,595 --> 00:00:49,425
and presented completely different performances.

20
00:00:50,125 --> 00:00:51,495
(If I try to die, I'll live.)

21
00:00:51,495 --> 00:00:53,065
(If I try to live, I'll die.)

22
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:54,995
(I'm going to try to die. That's my attitude.)

23
00:00:54,995 --> 00:00:56,635
(It was a matter of survival.)

24
00:00:56,635 --> 00:00:58,465
(I'll pull it off and never go home.)

25
00:00:58,465 --> 00:01:00,235
(I must...)

26
00:01:00,235 --> 00:01:01,235
(win again.)

27
00:01:01,805 --> 00:01:03,945
(Just send anyone among the other three.)

28
00:01:03,945 --> 00:01:04,945
(I don't care as long as it's not me.)

29
00:01:05,045 --> 00:01:06,705
Director NaiN completed an energetic performance...

30
00:01:06,705 --> 00:01:09,375
by making versatile use of the cubes.

31
00:01:10,985 --> 00:01:13,285
Director BABYZOO put on a powerful performance...

32
00:01:13,285 --> 00:01:16,215
by emphasizing his main genre, waacking.

33
00:01:19,025 --> 00:01:21,895
Director JEONG MIN JUN created three-dimensional scenes...

34
00:01:22,655 --> 00:01:25,465
by making harmony between the cubes and the dancers.

35
00:01:30,265 --> 00:01:31,265
(Exclaiming)

36
00:01:31,265 --> 00:01:32,265
By using the laser...

37
00:01:32,265 --> 00:01:34,475
and throwing the cubes,

38
00:01:34,475 --> 00:01:36,775
Director Kasper created an intense performance.

39
00:01:38,775 --> 00:01:41,115
After holding a survival competition...

40
00:01:41,275 --> 00:01:43,345
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

41
00:01:43,345 --> 00:01:46,545
(The second Last Stage: 24H)

42
00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:48,815
(NaiN and BABYZOO met as the final elimination candidates.)

43
00:01:49,385 --> 00:01:52,255
(NaiN is eliminated.)

44
00:01:52,625 --> 00:01:55,125
(Eliminated choreographer: NaiN)

45
00:01:55,395 --> 00:01:58,665
(In the second Last Stage: 24H, NaiN is eliminated.)

46
00:01:58,965 --> 00:02:00,735
(Oh, NaiN.)

47
00:02:00,735 --> 00:02:02,735
(This resulted...)

48
00:02:02,735 --> 00:02:05,735
(from what we focused on in the evaluation.)

49
00:02:05,735 --> 00:02:08,935
(This never means you were incapable as a director.)

50
00:02:08,935 --> 00:02:12,305
(NaiN put on a cool, happy performance before she left.)

51
00:02:12,305 --> 00:02:14,575
(That's what I wanted to tell you.)

52
00:02:14,575 --> 00:02:17,075
(Thank you.)

53
00:02:19,385 --> 00:02:22,085
(Good job. You did well.)

54
00:02:22,715 --> 00:02:27,655
(NaiN's journey ends here.)

55
00:02:27,655 --> 00:02:33,625
(You can watch Last Stage: 24H on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

56
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:35,395
(After another Last Stage ends...)

57
00:02:36,135 --> 00:02:37,905
(Sighing)

58
00:02:38,105 --> 00:02:40,775
(Entering her Director's Room for the last time)

59
00:02:40,935 --> 00:02:42,575
Goodbye.

60
00:02:43,405 --> 00:02:45,975
I'll have to take this back home.

61
00:02:45,975 --> 00:02:47,645
(Let me decorate my room.)

62
00:02:47,645 --> 00:02:49,145
(Ta-da!)

63
00:02:49,275 --> 00:02:53,985
(This is the "Street Dance Girls Fighter" winner trophy.)

64
00:02:53,985 --> 00:03:01,895
(She decorated her Director's Room herself.)

65
00:03:02,255 --> 00:03:03,525
NaiN.

66
00:03:03,795 --> 00:03:05,765
A letter for me? I should be the one writing to you.

67
00:03:05,765 --> 00:03:07,895
Why? NaiN.

68
00:03:07,895 --> 00:03:09,835
I feel so bad.

69
00:03:09,835 --> 00:03:12,135
If only I had done better,

70
00:03:12,135 --> 00:03:13,835
- this wouldn't have happened.
- Don't say that.

71
00:03:13,835 --> 00:03:15,935
That's how I feel.

72
00:03:16,075 --> 00:03:18,345
I have to face it.

73
00:03:18,345 --> 00:03:20,005
One thing is clear.

74
00:03:20,005 --> 00:03:21,645
Everything you've done here...

75
00:03:21,945 --> 00:03:23,575
was awesome.

76
00:03:23,575 --> 00:03:25,645
Really? Thank you.

77
00:03:31,585 --> 00:03:33,055
It's a present for you.

78
00:03:33,055 --> 00:03:36,495
- It's a kind of souvenir.
- Really? This is cute.

79
00:03:36,725 --> 00:03:37,795
(During the Title Sequence Film Mission)

80
00:03:37,795 --> 00:03:39,425
Your phone case is yellow.

81
00:03:39,425 --> 00:03:41,435
Yes. I like yellow.

82
00:03:41,565 --> 00:03:43,665
- My nails too.
- Your nails are yellow too.

83
00:03:43,935 --> 00:03:46,165
(He heard NaiN loves yellow by chance.)

84
00:03:46,365 --> 00:03:47,605
Since you like yellow.

85
00:03:47,605 --> 00:03:50,035
This is all I can do for you.

86
00:03:50,035 --> 00:03:51,845
I can't write a letter.

87
00:03:52,105 --> 00:03:53,545
I don't know how to.

88
00:03:54,245 --> 00:03:55,345
Thank you so much.

89
00:03:55,345 --> 00:03:56,675
Take it with you everywhere.

90
00:03:56,675 --> 00:03:57,685
Thank you.

91
00:03:57,685 --> 00:03:58,685
Well done.

92
00:03:58,685 --> 00:04:00,445
- Thank you.
- You were amazing.

93
00:04:00,445 --> 00:04:02,855
(The choreographers deliver their hearts in their own ways.)

94
00:04:03,925 --> 00:04:05,325
What Street World Fighter: Directors' War means to me?

95
00:04:05,925 --> 00:04:07,155
It was a turning point in my life.

96
00:04:07,825 --> 00:04:11,665
A turning point as I enter my mid-20s.

97
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:13,795
Wait a minute. What is this?

98
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,735
I'm here with the name NaiN.

99
00:04:15,735 --> 00:04:17,135
(She joined as Nain, not as a team.)

100
00:04:17,335 --> 00:04:20,905
I've never done anything half-heartedly even for a moment.

101
00:04:20,935 --> 00:04:24,205
(NaiN did her best every time.)

102
00:04:24,345 --> 00:04:27,945
I gave it my all, without any regrets.

103
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:30,015
I'm proud of myself.

104
00:04:30,015 --> 00:04:33,045
I was highly inspired and touched...

105
00:04:33,045 --> 00:04:35,885
by the fellow directors.

106
00:04:35,885 --> 00:04:39,625
It gave me a chance to grow a lot.

107
00:04:39,625 --> 00:04:42,195
I can't wait to see...

108
00:04:42,195 --> 00:04:45,225
how much my life's going to change...

109
00:04:45,225 --> 00:04:46,565
when I apply what I learned from this experience to my life.

110
00:04:47,025 --> 00:04:49,295
That will become...

111
00:04:49,295 --> 00:04:51,505
a huge turning point in my life.

112
00:04:53,365 --> 00:04:55,235
I had a great time.

113
00:04:56,705 --> 00:05:01,415
(NaiN leaves her Director's Room after showing her passion.)

114
00:05:01,615 --> 00:05:03,515
Cool. Nice view here.

115
00:05:03,515 --> 00:05:04,545
(Kasper and MIN JUN receive a strange envelope.)

116
00:05:04,545 --> 00:05:05,745
Is it another mission?

117
00:05:05,745 --> 00:05:07,585
- I've never had that before.
- What's that?

118
00:05:07,585 --> 00:05:09,455
"Kasper and JEONG MIN JUN came back alive."

119
00:05:09,455 --> 00:05:12,625
"Can you survive from 184m above ground?"

120
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:14,455
(Kasper is afraid of heights.)

121
00:05:14,655 --> 00:05:15,695
For real?

122
00:05:15,695 --> 00:05:17,155
(The highest in the world registered in the Guinness World Records)

123
00:05:17,155 --> 00:05:18,295
(Sky bridge observatory)

124
00:05:18,295 --> 00:05:19,825
(The extreme edge walk experience 184m above the ground)

125
00:05:19,825 --> 00:05:21,395
(Special training for the Last Stage survivals)

126
00:05:21,565 --> 00:05:22,765
(Entering after getting ready)

127
00:05:23,165 --> 00:05:24,165
(Groaning)

128
00:05:24,165 --> 00:05:25,605
(Everywhere...)

129
00:05:25,605 --> 00:05:27,265
(they look, )

130
00:05:27,265 --> 00:05:29,105
(the 184m high observatory is brutal.)

131
00:05:29,235 --> 00:05:30,745
Are we really doing this?

132
00:05:30,975 --> 00:05:32,005
(Putting on the safety gear)

133
00:05:32,005 --> 00:05:33,205
(It was safely filmed in the company of the professionals.)

134
00:05:33,505 --> 00:05:34,715
Once we're out there,

135
00:05:34,715 --> 00:05:35,945
we can't come back.

136
00:05:36,015 --> 00:05:37,345
(Help me.)

137
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:40,585
(Moving to the railing to try it)

138
00:05:40,815 --> 00:05:43,055
This is already so scary.

139
00:05:43,115 --> 00:05:44,855
(The view from 184m above the ground before their eyes)

140
00:05:45,025 --> 00:05:46,655
It's so windy.

141
00:05:47,025 --> 00:05:48,725
(He's just brave.)

142
00:05:48,725 --> 00:05:50,455
(This is where MIN JUN is standing.)

143
00:05:50,965 --> 00:05:52,925
(The boy born in 2004 is walking without crying.)

144
00:05:53,565 --> 00:05:55,635
(Laidback)

145
00:05:55,635 --> 00:05:59,705
(The boy born in 1992 is about to cry.)

146
00:06:00,305 --> 00:06:02,635
(He stays close to the wall and is barely moving.)

147
00:06:02,835 --> 00:06:04,705
MIN JUN, you're amazing.

148
00:06:04,705 --> 00:06:07,105
No wonder you survived two Last Stages.

149
00:06:07,105 --> 00:06:08,745
I should be registered in the world records.

150
00:06:08,745 --> 00:06:10,375
You should be.

151
00:06:10,845 --> 00:06:13,515
This is really scary.

152
00:06:13,685 --> 00:06:15,855
(What JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper are seeing)

153
00:06:15,855 --> 00:06:17,155
I'll explain what you're going to do now.

154
00:06:17,155 --> 00:06:18,725
You'll stand at the edge of the railing...

155
00:06:18,725 --> 00:06:20,425
with your heels out.

156
00:06:20,625 --> 00:06:21,625
(Horrified)

157
00:06:21,625 --> 00:06:24,465
Push your body and lean back.

158
00:06:24,795 --> 00:06:26,525
While doing that...

159
00:06:26,525 --> 00:06:27,535
(They have to get their hands off the rope.)

160
00:06:27,535 --> 00:06:28,635
(Dizzy)

161
00:06:28,635 --> 00:06:30,665
Wait.

162
00:06:30,665 --> 00:06:33,135
Do I really have to do this?

163
00:06:33,135 --> 00:06:34,705
I can't do it.

164
00:06:34,705 --> 00:06:36,475
Walk forward and line up with me.

165
00:06:36,475 --> 00:06:37,775
(Accepting his fate calmly)

166
00:06:38,005 --> 00:06:40,075
(Marching)

167
00:06:40,075 --> 00:06:41,145
(In denial)

168
00:06:41,145 --> 00:06:43,075
I can't do this.

169
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:45,045
(A terrifying view before his eyes)

170
00:06:45,345 --> 00:06:46,645
(Holding tight)

171
00:06:46,645 --> 00:06:48,215
Walk forward like me.

172
00:06:49,015 --> 00:06:50,255
(Plucking up his courage to step forward)

173
00:06:51,025 --> 00:06:52,055
(Finally taking a step forward)

174
00:06:52,055 --> 00:06:53,055
(Taking another step)

175
00:06:53,055 --> 00:06:54,525
(Just one more step!)

176
00:06:54,525 --> 00:06:55,695
(You can do it, Kasper.)

177
00:06:56,055 --> 00:06:57,825
(Marching toward the sea bravely)

178
00:06:57,825 --> 00:07:00,425
Good. Now, you're going to turn...

179
00:07:00,425 --> 00:07:02,335
and face the cameramen.

180
00:07:02,335 --> 00:07:05,305
(Another crisis)

181
00:07:05,305 --> 00:07:06,605
(Groaning)

182
00:07:06,765 --> 00:07:08,705
I feel miserable.

183
00:07:08,705 --> 00:07:09,705
(Drooping)

184
00:07:10,505 --> 00:07:12,375
Wait. This is too...

185
00:07:12,505 --> 00:07:14,315
Straighten your knees and lean.

186
00:07:14,315 --> 00:07:16,575
- Good.
- You're amazing.

187
00:07:16,745 --> 00:07:17,745
(Waving his hands)

188
00:07:17,745 --> 00:07:18,745
Good.

189
00:07:18,745 --> 00:07:20,715
(How can he do that?)

190
00:07:21,215 --> 00:07:23,115
(Kasper begins bending his knees.)

191
00:07:23,355 --> 00:07:24,685
(Losing his mind)

192
00:07:24,685 --> 00:07:26,985
Straighten your knees and lean.

193
00:07:26,985 --> 00:07:28,425
Straighten them.

194
00:07:29,055 --> 00:07:30,055
Good.

195
00:07:30,055 --> 00:07:31,665
I'll hold the rope.

196
00:07:31,665 --> 00:07:33,165
Let your hands go.

197
00:07:33,695 --> 00:07:35,435
Now, open your arm.

198
00:07:36,395 --> 00:07:38,405
- Gosh.
- It's okay. I got it.

199
00:07:39,335 --> 00:07:40,335
Good.

200
00:07:40,365 --> 00:07:41,375
Wait.

201
00:07:41,375 --> 00:07:43,135
(Kasper and MIN JUN succeed in leaning 184m above the ground.)

202
00:07:43,405 --> 00:07:44,445
That's good.

203
00:07:45,445 --> 00:07:46,845
(A photo to prove their survival 184m above the ground)

204
00:07:47,205 --> 00:07:48,445
(Trembling)

205
00:07:48,545 --> 00:07:49,975
(Another pose from BAILEY's choreography)

206
00:07:50,245 --> 00:07:52,345
(The two made dizzying memories.)

207
00:07:52,485 --> 00:07:54,115
(Returning after taking pictures)

208
00:07:54,255 --> 00:07:56,585
(Stunned)

209
00:07:57,755 --> 00:08:00,385
(Since when were we this close?)

210
00:08:00,485 --> 00:08:03,055
(Kasper freezes.)

211
00:08:03,055 --> 00:08:04,925
- Good job.
- You did it.

212
00:08:04,925 --> 00:08:06,965
(The two overcame their fears and pulled off a major challenge.)

213
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:09,395
That relieved the frustration inside.

214
00:08:09,395 --> 00:08:11,465
I'll pull off the next mission,

215
00:08:11,465 --> 00:08:14,475
so I can win.

216
00:08:14,475 --> 00:08:16,005
That gave me confidence.

217
00:08:16,005 --> 00:08:17,675
I'm going to work even harder.

218
00:08:17,675 --> 00:08:19,445
No more!

219
00:08:19,445 --> 00:08:21,215
Last Stage!

220
00:08:21,475 --> 00:08:23,145
Send everyone who ends up in the Last Stage.

221
00:08:23,145 --> 00:08:24,385
I'll pay for it.

222
00:08:24,885 --> 00:08:27,315
("Royalty" by Yoon Mi Rae and Tiger JK)

223
00:08:27,315 --> 00:08:31,525
(Directed by Back Koo Young)

224
00:09:23,505 --> 00:09:27,045
(To be continued)

225
00:09:27,915 --> 00:09:29,815
(The super kids direction mission went viral after it was revealed.)

226
00:09:29,815 --> 00:09:31,215
(From idols to kids?)

227
00:09:31,215 --> 00:09:33,085
(The man with parenting experience)

228
00:09:33,085 --> 00:09:34,085
(Out of my way!)

229
00:09:34,085 --> 00:09:35,085
(Devil in you)

230
00:09:35,485 --> 00:09:36,855
(It's funny how they can't control kids.)

231
00:09:36,855 --> 00:09:38,685
(That's hilarious.)

232
00:09:38,685 --> 00:09:39,755
(Giving up)

233
00:09:39,755 --> 00:09:40,955
(Simeez and BABYZOO have lost it.)

234
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,655
(Why do you keep looking at the ground?)

235
00:09:42,655 --> 00:09:43,655
(Flustered)

236
00:09:43,655 --> 00:09:44,665
(It's funny how he can't talk back and bites his lip.)

237
00:09:44,665 --> 00:09:45,665
(A kids battle?)

238
00:09:45,665 --> 00:09:46,995
(Super kids are here to turn the square upside down.)

239
00:09:46,995 --> 00:09:48,165
(Excited)

240
00:09:48,165 --> 00:09:49,165
(They're so cute.)

241
00:09:49,165 --> 00:09:50,535
(I don't know where to look.)

242
00:09:50,535 --> 00:09:53,905
(The Super Kids Dancer Casting Battle begins.)

243
00:09:54,675 --> 00:09:55,975
(Super class beyond imagination)

244
00:09:55,975 --> 00:09:56,975
(Thrilled)

245
00:09:56,975 --> 00:09:58,345
(He's like Bruce Lee.)

246
00:09:58,345 --> 00:09:59,745
(A series of marvelous dancing that stuns the grown-ups)

247
00:09:59,745 --> 00:10:02,245
(How can he be so flexible?)

248
00:10:02,245 --> 00:10:03,845
(Look at his moves. That's crazy.)

249
00:10:03,845 --> 00:10:05,845
(Kids continue to give them a heart attack.)

250
00:10:05,845 --> 00:10:06,845
(Throbbing)

251
00:10:06,845 --> 00:10:07,855
(I'm in love.)

252
00:10:07,855 --> 00:10:09,185
(Kids dancer casting meeting)

253
00:10:09,185 --> 00:10:10,285
(The 4-people team takes a long time to decide.)

254
00:10:10,285 --> 00:10:11,855
(What's good about having 4 people in the team is...)

255
00:10:11,855 --> 00:10:13,425
(that we get one more idea.)

256
00:10:13,425 --> 00:10:16,025
(What's bad is...)

257
00:10:16,025 --> 00:10:17,595
(there's another opinion.)

258
00:10:17,595 --> 00:10:19,525
(Why is it so hard to come to an agreement?)

259
00:10:19,525 --> 00:10:20,865
(We're having a hard time uniting.)

260
00:10:20,865 --> 00:10:23,065
(It's called a team match, but it's basically an individual match.)

261
00:10:23,065 --> 00:10:25,965
(Super Kids Direct Mission was even harder...)

262
00:10:25,965 --> 00:10:30,605
(because it was their first time.)

263
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:34,375
(That's awesome!)

264
00:10:34,375 --> 00:10:35,375
(I think they're going to win.)

265
00:10:35,375 --> 00:10:37,175
(It's about time to surprise people.)

266
00:10:38,915 --> 00:10:40,145
(That's what I'm talking about.)

267
00:10:40,745 --> 00:10:42,085
(See? I had to surprise them.)

268
00:10:42,315 --> 00:10:44,455
(Who will enter the semifinal...)

269
00:10:44,455 --> 00:10:48,355
(and who will head to the Last Stage?)

270
00:10:52,425 --> 00:10:55,735
(That broke my heart big time.)

271
00:10:56,095 --> 00:10:58,035
(You can watch Last Stage: 24H on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

272
00:10:58,035 --> 00:10:59,805
- Hello.
- Hello.

273
00:10:59,805 --> 00:11:01,875
I'm back to the battlefield.

274
00:11:02,135 --> 00:11:03,135
(Back to the Director's Room)

275
00:11:03,135 --> 00:11:04,175
It's been a while.

276
00:11:04,745 --> 00:11:06,805
I'm already back for the next mission.

277
00:11:07,105 --> 00:11:09,575
Time really flies.

278
00:11:10,115 --> 00:11:12,045
I've been trying to recover...

279
00:11:12,345 --> 00:11:14,485
and pull off my schedule.

280
00:11:14,485 --> 00:11:16,555
I joined as a judge.

281
00:11:17,085 --> 00:11:18,385
There were many kid dancers.

282
00:11:18,485 --> 00:11:20,885
They were around 13 or 14.

283
00:11:21,155 --> 00:11:23,425
I want to teach them.

284
00:11:23,525 --> 00:11:24,665
Every student from my academy...

285
00:11:24,665 --> 00:11:26,725
will be known as incredible dancers.

286
00:11:27,025 --> 00:11:28,795
I'd be happy.

287
00:11:29,365 --> 00:11:30,635
I didn't think you'd like kids.

288
00:11:30,795 --> 00:11:31,965
I don't.

289
00:11:32,405 --> 00:11:34,935
My nephew is so cute. I miss him already.

290
00:11:35,335 --> 00:11:36,475
What are we doing?

291
00:11:38,105 --> 00:11:40,075
I was planning to stay calm, but I'm startled again.

292
00:11:40,305 --> 00:11:41,475
(No!)

293
00:11:41,815 --> 00:11:44,345
Finally. Here it comes.

294
00:11:44,845 --> 00:11:45,915
Let's go.

295
00:11:45,915 --> 00:11:47,615
I haven't heard the siren in a while.

296
00:11:47,685 --> 00:11:51,385
(What's the next mission at the fourth crossroads of fate?)

297
00:11:51,885 --> 00:11:54,855
(All 7 choreographers are seated.)

298
00:11:54,855 --> 00:11:56,395
Seven choreographers...

299
00:11:56,395 --> 00:11:59,065
competed for their reputation.

300
00:11:59,425 --> 00:12:02,165
They'll compete once again to prove their directing skills.

301
00:12:02,295 --> 00:12:05,205
The next mission will be their new challenge.

302
00:12:05,505 --> 00:12:07,035
Just thinking about it terrifies me.

303
00:12:07,105 --> 00:12:09,135
It was totally unpredictable.

304
00:12:09,235 --> 00:12:10,335
I was anxious.

305
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:12,175
Here it is.

306
00:12:12,605 --> 00:12:13,645
What's it going to be?

307
00:12:13,745 --> 00:12:15,545
I couldn't predict what the mission was going to be.

308
00:12:15,545 --> 00:12:16,715
The mega crew mission for sure.

309
00:12:16,875 --> 00:12:18,815
- My heart is in pain.
- Hello.

310
00:12:19,615 --> 00:12:21,185
- What?
- Hello.

311
00:12:22,015 --> 00:12:23,055
- My heart is in pain.
- Hello.

312
00:12:24,555 --> 00:12:25,685
- Hello.
- What's that?

313
00:12:27,455 --> 00:12:30,695
Hello. I'm ShiN from Japan.

314
00:12:30,895 --> 00:12:32,565
I'm 12 years old.

315
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:34,025
- Hello.
- What's going on?

316
00:12:34,495 --> 00:12:36,735
- What? Are we working with kids?
- I'm not sure about this.

317
00:12:37,635 --> 00:12:39,435
We're dancers from Japan.

318
00:12:39,435 --> 00:12:41,105
- We're dancers.
- Kid dancers?

319
00:12:41,105 --> 00:12:43,575
- Kid dancers?
- It's a kids mega crew mission.

320
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:45,675
I was dumbfounded. I was like, "What's happening?"

321
00:12:45,945 --> 00:12:47,575
I'm Third Bro, a b-boy from China.

322
00:12:47,645 --> 00:12:48,945
I'm Song Haoming from China.

323
00:12:48,945 --> 00:12:51,215
- He's cute.
- My name is s, o, So.

324
00:12:51,485 --> 00:12:53,185
Chinese dancers are amazing.

325
00:12:53,315 --> 00:12:54,885
I'm Jack.B. I'm 13.

326
00:12:54,885 --> 00:12:55,885
It's Jack.B.

327
00:12:55,885 --> 00:12:58,555
I know them. They were in my class.

328
00:12:58,855 --> 00:13:01,025
- No way.
- I was becoming more certain.

329
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:03,995
Those who will join the directors for this mission are...

330
00:13:04,095 --> 00:13:07,095
Us, global kid dancers.

331
00:13:07,895 --> 00:13:08,895
Gosh.

332
00:13:09,135 --> 00:13:10,135
(Getting up)

333
00:13:10,295 --> 00:13:11,965
I'm shocked.

334
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:14,065
I never saw that coming.

335
00:13:14,065 --> 00:13:15,605
(Losing her mind)

336
00:13:15,605 --> 00:13:16,875
This mission is...

337
00:13:17,405 --> 00:13:19,175
the Super Kids Direct Mission.

338
00:13:19,345 --> 00:13:21,645
Direct the Next Generation.

339
00:13:21,845 --> 00:13:23,815
- Really?
- You're lying.

340
00:13:24,045 --> 00:13:26,885
I'm directing a super kid every day.

341
00:13:27,815 --> 00:13:29,385
- Right.
- Last night,

342
00:13:29,385 --> 00:13:31,525
this morning. Every single day.

343
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:34,225
You're giving a kids direct mission...

344
00:13:34,285 --> 00:13:36,455
when I'm directing a kid every day?

345
00:13:36,695 --> 00:13:38,125
I thought it was a prank.

346
00:13:38,465 --> 00:13:40,395
I've never seen this anywhere before.

347
00:13:40,565 --> 00:13:42,865
I never saw that coming.

348
00:13:42,865 --> 00:13:44,335
It's the first time...

349
00:13:44,335 --> 00:13:45,835
in the history of this series.

350
00:13:45,835 --> 00:13:47,135
I surrender.

351
00:13:47,205 --> 00:13:48,605
It's funny though.

352
00:13:49,605 --> 00:13:51,135
Because they're still growing,

353
00:13:51,135 --> 00:13:53,945
kid dancers have infinite potential.

354
00:13:54,145 --> 00:13:57,645
You'll go beyond judging their current level...

355
00:13:57,715 --> 00:13:59,385
and discover their unique strengths...

356
00:13:59,585 --> 00:14:01,085
and potential.

357
00:14:01,085 --> 00:14:04,485
You'll guide them to bring out their potential...

358
00:14:04,625 --> 00:14:07,055
and capture it all on film.

359
00:14:07,355 --> 00:14:09,755
You'll face who you truly are.

360
00:14:10,525 --> 00:14:12,495
Stress and patience.

361
00:14:12,495 --> 00:14:14,325
That's going to be the tough part.

362
00:14:14,465 --> 00:14:16,265
I wonder if the other choreographers understand how hard it is.

363
00:14:16,735 --> 00:14:18,065
I'm devastated.

364
00:14:18,305 --> 00:14:20,135
I'm not sure I can meet them at their level.

365
00:14:20,335 --> 00:14:22,875
Simeez might struggle with it.

366
00:14:23,005 --> 00:14:24,645
She has no intention of meeting them at their level.

367
00:14:24,705 --> 00:14:27,445
I teach pretty fast.

368
00:14:27,445 --> 00:14:29,245
"Are you ready to do this together?"

369
00:14:29,345 --> 00:14:30,515
I can't do that.

370
00:14:30,515 --> 00:14:31,815
This isn't going to be easy.

371
00:14:31,815 --> 00:14:34,015
Wait!

372
00:14:34,115 --> 00:14:35,315
Kids. Wait.

373
00:14:35,415 --> 00:14:37,255
(Simeez having a mental breakdown is coming soon.)

374
00:14:37,255 --> 00:14:39,385
I'm actually worried about Kasper.

375
00:14:39,755 --> 00:14:41,355
I love this mission.

376
00:14:41,595 --> 00:14:45,295
I've always wanted to teach kids.

377
00:14:45,295 --> 00:14:46,495
I'm intrigued by it.

378
00:14:48,435 --> 00:14:49,635
(Father Kasper is coming soon.)

379
00:14:49,635 --> 00:14:51,705
The one who's going to be best at it?

380
00:14:51,705 --> 00:14:53,365
Either BADA or BABYZOO.

381
00:14:53,505 --> 00:14:54,975
BABYZOO looks like he'd be good at it.

382
00:14:55,135 --> 00:14:56,335
"Guys, let's go."

383
00:14:56,335 --> 00:14:57,705
"Again."

384
00:14:57,775 --> 00:14:59,305
"Guys, do you want to do this 100 times?"

385
00:14:59,405 --> 00:15:02,745
(Again)

386
00:15:02,745 --> 00:15:04,345
(BABYZOO the clear-eyed maniac is coming soon.)

387
00:15:04,375 --> 00:15:05,515
I'm experienced.

388
00:15:06,285 --> 00:15:08,415
I taught elementary school boys...

389
00:15:08,415 --> 00:15:10,415
for two years.

390
00:15:10,415 --> 00:15:11,855
That's amazing experience.

391
00:15:11,855 --> 00:15:13,855
I know what they like.

392
00:15:13,855 --> 00:15:15,855
I know when they lose focus.

393
00:15:15,855 --> 00:15:18,965
I think those memories will help me.

394
00:15:18,965 --> 00:15:20,165
You look like you'll be good at it.

395
00:15:20,225 --> 00:15:23,535
They probably know BADA.

396
00:15:23,535 --> 00:15:25,105
Regardless, being experienced...

397
00:15:25,105 --> 00:15:26,605
makes a big difference.

398
00:15:26,605 --> 00:15:27,975
My strength is...

399
00:15:27,975 --> 00:15:31,405
the memories of my youth that I still have.

400
00:15:31,405 --> 00:15:33,045
Hey, we have them too.

401
00:15:33,045 --> 00:15:34,745
We still have them too.

402
00:15:34,745 --> 00:15:36,075
I remember them too!

403
00:15:36,315 --> 00:15:38,345
(The young boy is flustered.)

404
00:15:38,345 --> 00:15:40,245
- I remember them too!
- He often says that.

405
00:15:40,345 --> 00:15:41,655
I can't imagine MIN JUN directing them.

406
00:15:41,885 --> 00:15:44,685
I don't know if kids will be able to pull off MIN JUN's style.

407
00:15:44,925 --> 00:15:48,195
It's up to MIN JUN to lead kids to pull it off.

408
00:15:48,425 --> 00:15:50,295
This mission will be...

409
00:15:50,525 --> 00:15:52,395
There's an odd number of us.

410
00:15:52,395 --> 00:15:53,665
So I'm expecting an individual match.

411
00:15:53,825 --> 00:15:55,695
The Super Kids Direct Mission...

412
00:15:56,395 --> 00:15:57,665
will be a team match.

413
00:15:57,865 --> 00:15:58,865
- I knew it.
- What?

414
00:15:58,865 --> 00:15:59,905
Yay.

415
00:15:59,905 --> 00:16:01,505
I'm not good with kids.

416
00:16:01,505 --> 00:16:04,075
I thought we could help each other out.

417
00:16:04,075 --> 00:16:06,875
I'd happy to work with anyone.

418
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:08,975
I'm not exactly into a team match.

419
00:16:09,145 --> 00:16:11,685
Everyone has different perspectives and opinions.

420
00:16:11,885 --> 00:16:14,015
We might not agree. We might not get along.

421
00:16:14,245 --> 00:16:17,085
It might be difficult for us to reach an agreement.

422
00:16:17,185 --> 00:16:19,125
But there are seven of us.

423
00:16:19,285 --> 00:16:20,455
How are we going to form teams?

424
00:16:20,455 --> 00:16:22,425
The teams will be decided...

425
00:16:22,695 --> 00:16:23,695
What is it?

426
00:16:25,125 --> 00:16:27,795
based on the concept paper you wrote.

427
00:16:27,965 --> 00:16:29,035
What?

428
00:16:29,265 --> 00:16:30,465
What does that mean?

429
00:16:30,965 --> 00:16:33,105
You'll move to your Director's Room...

430
00:16:33,105 --> 00:16:35,705
and complete the concept paper.

431
00:16:35,805 --> 00:16:38,375
The best masterpiece is the story.

432
00:16:38,575 --> 00:16:42,115
I'm afraid my concept and story might be a bit childish.

433
00:16:42,115 --> 00:16:43,115
What should I do?

434
00:16:43,115 --> 00:16:45,845
Oh, my gosh. What am I going to do with the kids?

435
00:16:46,015 --> 00:16:47,585
(7 choreographers complete the concept paper.)

436
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:48,815
I wondered how teams were divided...

437
00:16:48,815 --> 00:16:50,615
based on the concept paper.

438
00:16:50,615 --> 00:16:51,655
By presenting it?

439
00:16:51,725 --> 00:16:54,185
Each choreographer will receive...

440
00:16:54,185 --> 00:16:57,655
six concept papers without the names excluding your own.

441
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:00,265
Solely based on the concept paper,

442
00:17:00,365 --> 00:17:04,595
pick top two concepts...

443
00:17:04,805 --> 00:17:08,535
that are expected to be the best.

444
00:17:08,905 --> 00:17:10,435
It was important.

445
00:17:10,575 --> 00:17:13,075
Judging by the concept? That's fair.

446
00:17:13,205 --> 00:17:14,575
After everyone makes their choices,

447
00:17:14,875 --> 00:17:18,645
the writer of the most chosen concept paper...

448
00:17:19,115 --> 00:17:21,145
will decide the team.

449
00:17:21,145 --> 00:17:22,155
(Unbelievable)

450
00:17:22,155 --> 00:17:23,515
This time...

451
00:17:23,515 --> 00:17:25,125
I want to decide on my own team.

452
00:17:25,255 --> 00:17:27,025
I love power.

453
00:17:27,025 --> 00:17:29,755
I did think that it would be great to be able to decide.

454
00:17:29,895 --> 00:17:33,225
The team decider will decide whether to finish the piece...

455
00:17:33,225 --> 00:17:36,095
as a 3-man team or 4-man team.

456
00:17:36,235 --> 00:17:39,205
Without knowing who the writer is,

457
00:17:39,365 --> 00:17:41,575
the concepts will be chosen...

458
00:17:41,575 --> 00:17:43,475
to form the team.

459
00:17:43,635 --> 00:17:45,175
The remaining choreographers...

460
00:17:45,275 --> 00:17:48,005
will automatically be formed as the opposing team.

461
00:17:48,245 --> 00:17:50,075
Being able to choose my own team...

462
00:17:50,075 --> 00:17:51,885
means a dream team can be formed...

463
00:17:51,885 --> 00:17:53,045
when there are good concepts.

464
00:17:53,245 --> 00:17:54,785
I can't be sure if it's someone I wish to work with...

465
00:17:54,785 --> 00:17:55,885
since the names won't be revealed.

466
00:17:55,885 --> 00:17:58,925
I thought that my concept was quite obvious.

467
00:17:58,925 --> 00:18:01,655
I think I can figure out the other concepts as well.

468
00:18:01,755 --> 00:18:03,895
Based on the number of team members,

469
00:18:03,895 --> 00:18:06,425
each team will split their piece into chapters.

470
00:18:06,665 --> 00:18:09,595
Each choreographer must be in charge of each chapter...

471
00:18:09,695 --> 00:18:14,305
and take care of the concept, music, choreography, and directing.

472
00:18:14,435 --> 00:18:18,905
Each chapter must be at least 40 seconds.

473
00:18:19,005 --> 00:18:20,145
- I see.
- I see.

474
00:18:20,145 --> 00:18:22,515
While putting together a piece as a team,

475
00:18:22,545 --> 00:18:24,985
each person will be evaluated personally...

476
00:18:25,145 --> 00:18:28,085
as a director of each chapter.

477
00:18:28,155 --> 00:18:30,385
It's a team battle, but we're all against each other.

478
00:18:30,655 --> 00:18:32,385
It's one piece,

479
00:18:32,385 --> 00:18:35,895
but there has to be something that stands out.

480
00:18:36,055 --> 00:18:37,255
It has to be tasty.

481
00:18:37,255 --> 00:18:39,395
There should be an impact when my chapter plays.

482
00:18:39,595 --> 00:18:41,065
This mission...

483
00:18:41,165 --> 00:18:43,495
will be evaluated by the Fight Judges.

484
00:18:43,665 --> 00:18:45,105
The choreographers on the same team...

485
00:18:45,105 --> 00:18:47,205
will earn the same team score.

486
00:18:47,205 --> 00:18:49,605
The team score and personal score will be added together...

487
00:18:49,605 --> 00:18:51,605
to become the final score.

488
00:18:51,705 --> 00:18:53,345
Based on these scores,

489
00:18:53,345 --> 00:18:55,615
the personal ranks will be decided from 1st place to 7th place.

490
00:18:55,815 --> 00:18:57,915
The personal scores will have a greater significance...

491
00:18:58,115 --> 00:19:01,315
that the team scores.

492
00:19:02,655 --> 00:19:03,885
Gosh, that's harsh.

493
00:19:04,155 --> 00:19:06,855
It's an individual game pretending to be a team game.

494
00:19:07,055 --> 00:19:10,855
The team scores are less significant than the individual scores.

495
00:19:11,095 --> 00:19:12,865
It means the focus is on the individual in the end.

496
00:19:12,895 --> 00:19:14,865
It's still important to meet good team members.

497
00:19:14,865 --> 00:19:18,205
There's a big disadvantage if the team fails to win.

498
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,735
Winning is a must.

499
00:19:19,835 --> 00:19:21,105
The choreographer...

500
00:19:21,235 --> 00:19:24,275
who fails to prove their directing skills in this mission...

501
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:27,175
will have to prove their will to survive...

502
00:19:27,175 --> 00:19:30,345
by entering Last Stage: 24H.

503
00:19:30,475 --> 00:19:32,245
I tried not to be afraid of it.

504
00:19:32,245 --> 00:19:33,815
But I think I'm afraid of it.

505
00:19:34,345 --> 00:19:35,415
I didn't want to be there.

506
00:19:36,085 --> 00:19:37,315
I don't want to be there.

507
00:19:37,315 --> 00:19:40,955
The number of choreographers who will head to Last Stage: 24H...

508
00:19:41,285 --> 00:19:42,495
- How many will it be?
- Two?

509
00:19:42,655 --> 00:19:43,655
Three?

510
00:19:45,395 --> 00:19:46,425
is four.

511
00:19:46,695 --> 00:19:47,865
(Last Stage: 24H)

512
00:19:47,925 --> 00:19:48,935
- What?
- What?

513
00:19:49,095 --> 00:19:50,595
It's the rest except for three?

514
00:19:50,635 --> 00:19:52,005
Only three will survive? That's a low chance.

515
00:19:52,005 --> 00:19:53,005
(Shocked)

516
00:19:53,135 --> 00:19:55,205
If it's more than half out of seven,

517
00:19:55,205 --> 00:19:56,475
it can always be me.

518
00:19:56,575 --> 00:19:58,675
I've already been there once. Even if I do end up there...

519
00:19:58,845 --> 00:20:01,305
I never want to be there! Never!

520
00:20:01,715 --> 00:20:02,715
I'm in danger.

521
00:20:02,715 --> 00:20:05,685
Shouldn't I be preparing for the Last Stage instead?

522
00:20:05,885 --> 00:20:07,145
It was really harsh.

523
00:20:07,585 --> 00:20:09,255
"No, BADA. You won't end up there."

524
00:20:09,455 --> 00:20:13,685
Becoming the team decider will be very important.

525
00:20:13,925 --> 00:20:17,295
Now, you must head over to your Directors' Rooms...

526
00:20:17,455 --> 00:20:21,065
and choose two concept papers.

527
00:20:21,365 --> 00:20:22,735
I can't wait to see what I'll find.

528
00:20:22,735 --> 00:20:24,195
People will definitely like my concept.

529
00:20:24,195 --> 00:20:28,575
I did think that my concept was the most intuitive and on point.

530
00:20:28,575 --> 00:20:30,775
This is my cheat code.

531
00:20:30,835 --> 00:20:32,105
"Being myself."

532
00:20:32,175 --> 00:20:34,175
I came up with a good concept.

533
00:20:34,405 --> 00:20:36,745
I had to decide on the 1st and 2nd priorities.

534
00:20:36,745 --> 00:20:40,315
I thought about the standards I should base them on.

535
00:20:40,845 --> 00:20:42,385
That was it?

536
00:20:42,385 --> 00:20:43,685
It really threw me off.

537
00:20:43,785 --> 00:20:45,185
This is driving me crazy.

538
00:20:45,185 --> 00:20:46,225
Here they are.

539
00:20:46,225 --> 00:20:47,355
(The anonymous concept papers were sent to each room.)

540
00:20:47,355 --> 00:20:48,655
Everyone did a good job.

541
00:20:48,795 --> 00:20:50,425
I didn't think this was this important.

542
00:20:50,425 --> 00:20:52,265
The team selection is crucial.

543
00:20:52,265 --> 00:20:53,865
I should've worked a bit harder.

544
00:20:53,865 --> 00:20:57,165
We can't know the writers of the concept papers,

545
00:20:57,165 --> 00:21:02,105
but we can understand the quality of the piece they wish to make.

546
00:21:02,275 --> 00:21:04,535
I would've done a better job if I had known.

547
00:21:05,275 --> 00:21:08,175
To be honest, I think the others will know it's me.

548
00:21:08,545 --> 00:21:09,715
"Musicality."

549
00:21:10,015 --> 00:21:11,045
(Musicality)

550
00:21:11,045 --> 00:21:13,545
(Kapser's trait: He always talks about musicality.)

551
00:21:13,845 --> 00:21:14,885
"Musicality."

552
00:21:15,285 --> 00:21:17,585
The others are musical instruments...

553
00:21:17,585 --> 00:21:20,325
and I'm the conductor who leads them.

554
00:21:20,455 --> 00:21:22,095
This sounds like Kasper based on the title.

555
00:21:22,095 --> 00:21:23,825
I think this one is Kasper's.

556
00:21:23,925 --> 00:21:26,265
Kasper is the only one who wants to become a conductor.

557
00:21:26,265 --> 00:21:28,795
He wants to form an orchestra?

558
00:21:28,895 --> 00:21:29,895
It's so predictable.

559
00:21:30,265 --> 00:21:32,365
"Musicality" seems to be Tae Woo's.

560
00:21:32,435 --> 00:21:34,565
It's so predictable. I will put this one away.

561
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,905
This one is the longest. "Born to Be Stars."

562
00:21:37,005 --> 00:21:38,575
"Born to Be Stars."

563
00:21:38,675 --> 00:21:42,115
"Dancing like crazy." This phrase made it feel like...

564
00:21:42,115 --> 00:21:43,645
it was BABYZOO's.

565
00:21:43,645 --> 00:21:46,015
Just his name is missing. All of this is BABYZOO.

566
00:21:46,015 --> 00:21:47,545
He's a born-to-be star.

567
00:21:47,645 --> 00:21:49,615
It was based on my story.

568
00:21:49,855 --> 00:21:53,325
While watching fancy dancers and celebrities on TV,

569
00:21:53,325 --> 00:21:54,355
I developed an interest in dancing.

570
00:21:54,355 --> 00:21:56,695
I wanted to share my story.

571
00:21:56,855 --> 00:21:59,995
"After waking up from the dream, the dream is written on..."

572
00:21:59,995 --> 00:22:01,365
I never do things like these.

573
00:22:01,765 --> 00:22:02,835
This is what it's like.

574
00:22:03,395 --> 00:22:04,395
Gosh!

575
00:22:04,395 --> 00:22:05,635
(The child wakes up from his dream.)

576
00:22:06,135 --> 00:22:07,135
My dream...

577
00:22:07,505 --> 00:22:08,835
is to become a super dancer!

578
00:22:09,405 --> 00:22:11,005
That's how it ends.

579
00:22:11,535 --> 00:22:13,345
Gosh! I can't do this!

580
00:22:13,575 --> 00:22:14,605
"Home."

581
00:22:14,945 --> 00:22:17,345
It's based on war.

582
00:22:17,575 --> 00:22:20,115
It wishes all children to be able to return home.

583
00:22:20,285 --> 00:22:21,855
"Paradise." The background is an orphanage...

584
00:22:21,855 --> 00:22:23,885
or a community of children.

585
00:22:23,885 --> 00:22:26,055
This one is also a heavy topic.

586
00:22:26,055 --> 00:22:28,285
The topics are heavier than I expected.

587
00:22:28,285 --> 00:22:31,225
I wanted to talk about a child's experience.

588
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:33,625
"Do you want to go to the secret playground with me?"

589
00:22:33,795 --> 00:22:36,465
It's a playground full of pure innocence.

590
00:22:36,465 --> 00:22:38,965
Anyone has a sense of innocence inside of them.

591
00:22:38,965 --> 00:22:42,035
I wanted to make people live through those moments...

592
00:22:42,035 --> 00:22:44,875
through children.

593
00:22:44,875 --> 00:22:49,245
My expressions might seem rough and sharp,

594
00:22:49,245 --> 00:22:52,485
but I've always danced with an innocent heart.

595
00:22:52,715 --> 00:22:55,855
I think everyone will enjoy the playground or hideout.

596
00:22:55,855 --> 00:22:57,155
I don't want to go to the playground.

597
00:22:57,455 --> 00:22:59,585
The location must be set for this one.

598
00:22:59,585 --> 00:23:02,425
"School and uniform." I think I should avoid...

599
00:23:02,425 --> 00:23:04,025
these one-dimensional words.

600
00:23:04,225 --> 00:23:05,225
Hold on.

601
00:23:05,725 --> 00:23:07,895
Isn't this too simple? "Friends."

602
00:23:08,165 --> 00:23:09,295
"We become with the language of dancing..."

603
00:23:09,295 --> 00:23:10,935
"even though we speak different languages."

604
00:23:10,935 --> 00:23:13,065
This sounds like a campaign slogan.

605
00:23:13,065 --> 00:23:14,505
instead of being a concept or story.

606
00:23:14,505 --> 00:23:16,735
All right. The next one is "The Unknown World."

607
00:23:16,875 --> 00:23:18,745
This one is hard to understand.

608
00:23:18,745 --> 00:23:20,345
The story doesn't stand out.

609
00:23:20,345 --> 00:23:21,405
It's too vague.

610
00:23:21,545 --> 00:23:22,545
My top priority is "Friends."

611
00:23:22,545 --> 00:23:23,575
My second priority is "The Unknown World."

612
00:23:23,745 --> 00:23:25,385
It's the same for the other four.

613
00:23:25,385 --> 00:23:28,185
If the focus is too strong on the message,

614
00:23:28,185 --> 00:23:29,585
I feel like it will make us feel trapped.

615
00:23:29,585 --> 00:23:31,855
I went for the simple ones.

616
00:23:31,855 --> 00:23:34,155
I'll choose the playground one as my top priority.

617
00:23:34,485 --> 00:23:36,725
I think it will be convenient to split it into chapters.

618
00:23:36,795 --> 00:23:38,195
I want to work with BABYZOO.

619
00:23:38,295 --> 00:23:39,695
Should I just pick "Born to Be Stars?"

620
00:23:39,695 --> 00:23:42,665
I went with a deep concept as my top priority.

621
00:23:42,665 --> 00:23:44,165
My second priority is a simple one.

622
00:23:44,165 --> 00:23:47,535
I think "Born to Be Stars" will be easier to understand.

623
00:23:47,605 --> 00:23:48,775
(The choreographers chose their priorities with their own plans.)

624
00:23:48,775 --> 00:23:51,075
Which concept paper...

625
00:23:51,075 --> 00:23:53,105
will get the most votes?

626
00:23:53,245 --> 00:23:54,445
(Super Kids Direct Mission)

627
00:23:54,705 --> 00:23:56,745
(Team decider, INGYOO)

628
00:23:57,045 --> 00:23:58,945
(INGYOO placed 1st?)

629
00:23:59,445 --> 00:24:01,185
It's INGYOO?

630
00:24:01,955 --> 00:24:03,785
It's Choreographer INGYOO's piece,

631
00:24:04,155 --> 00:24:06,485
"Do You Want to Go to the Secret Playground With Me?"

632
00:24:06,485 --> 00:24:07,485
(It was INGYOO's!)

633
00:24:07,485 --> 00:24:08,995
It was INGYOO's.

634
00:24:09,125 --> 00:24:11,355
INGYOO is the team decider.

635
00:24:11,425 --> 00:24:13,025
Please head to the Directors' Room...

636
00:24:13,025 --> 00:24:14,995
and put together your team...

637
00:24:14,995 --> 00:24:17,495
for the Super Kids Direct Mission.

638
00:24:17,565 --> 00:24:18,765
That must be great.

639
00:24:19,105 --> 00:24:22,075
Hold on! I don't know the owners of the concept papers anyway.

640
00:24:22,305 --> 00:24:23,305
This is crazy.

641
00:24:23,305 --> 00:24:25,505
He has to decide without knowing the names?

642
00:24:26,045 --> 00:24:28,475
(The team decider is lost in thought.)

643
00:24:28,615 --> 00:24:30,475
I want to work with MIN JUN this time.

644
00:24:30,475 --> 00:24:32,445
MIN JUN always had a big impact...

645
00:24:32,445 --> 00:24:34,015
when it came to storytelling.

646
00:24:34,015 --> 00:24:35,255
I want to work with INGYOO.

647
00:24:35,315 --> 00:24:36,715
You must be sick of INGYOO, Hee Jung.

648
00:24:36,715 --> 00:24:38,055
You worked with him for the previous one.

649
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:39,925
It might feel predictable,

650
00:24:39,925 --> 00:24:42,695
but working with Simeez will never go wrong.

651
00:24:42,825 --> 00:24:46,465
I think BADA will do a tasty job with the group dance.

652
00:24:46,495 --> 00:24:48,495
INGYOO should work with Kasper.

653
00:24:48,735 --> 00:24:51,065
That will be fun to watch.

654
00:24:51,135 --> 00:24:52,565
I didn't choose his concept.

655
00:24:52,835 --> 00:24:54,135
I didn't go to the playground.

656
00:24:54,235 --> 00:24:56,275
INGYOO and Kasper's clash chemistry?

657
00:24:56,675 --> 00:24:58,075
Gosh, this is driving me crazy.

658
00:24:58,435 --> 00:24:59,975
How am I supposed to decide just by these?

659
00:25:00,805 --> 00:25:03,075
The way I see it, "Musicality,"

660
00:25:03,075 --> 00:25:04,815
"Friends," and "The Unknown World..."

661
00:25:04,815 --> 00:25:06,515
were written by simple people.

662
00:25:06,615 --> 00:25:08,755
"Home," "Paradise," and "Born to Be Stars."

663
00:25:08,755 --> 00:25:10,985
These people have solid storylines...

664
00:25:10,985 --> 00:25:13,025
and can be writers.

665
00:25:13,025 --> 00:25:15,325
In these team missions, writers are needed.

666
00:25:15,325 --> 00:25:16,425
I'll go with these.

667
00:25:16,925 --> 00:25:18,155
What kind of decision did INGYOO make?

668
00:25:18,255 --> 00:25:19,325
I want to work with him.

669
00:25:19,395 --> 00:25:20,595
I'm sure it won't be me.

670
00:25:20,595 --> 00:25:21,625
(Super Kids Direct Mission: Team decider, INGYOO)

671
00:25:21,625 --> 00:25:22,765
("Friends" is his first choice.)

672
00:25:22,765 --> 00:25:24,395
It's "Friends." Who is this?

673
00:25:24,395 --> 00:25:25,405
I'm not sure.

674
00:25:25,835 --> 00:25:26,905
Who do you think it will be?

675
00:25:26,905 --> 00:25:28,505
The content was too simple.

676
00:25:28,505 --> 00:25:31,275
I couldn't tell who wrote this.

677
00:25:31,335 --> 00:25:32,505
Doesn't it feel like BABYZOO's?

678
00:25:32,505 --> 00:25:34,105
(Who is the owner of "Friends?")

679
00:25:34,105 --> 00:25:35,445
("Friends" by BADA)

680
00:25:36,045 --> 00:25:37,945
- Gosh!
- Gosh!

681
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:39,515
It was BADA!

682
00:25:39,515 --> 00:25:41,285
I didn't expect it to be her.

683
00:25:41,645 --> 00:25:44,715
I felt happy because I chose INGYOO's.

684
00:25:44,715 --> 00:25:46,325
We were able to choose each other.

685
00:25:46,325 --> 00:25:47,385
Right.

686
00:25:47,385 --> 00:25:48,485
(Good thing he didn't choose mine.)

687
00:25:48,825 --> 00:25:49,895
Who else did he pick?

688
00:25:50,025 --> 00:25:51,055
The next one.

689
00:25:51,055 --> 00:25:52,495
("The Unknown World" by Simeez)

690
00:25:52,825 --> 00:25:54,095
(He's satisfied again.)

691
00:25:54,095 --> 00:25:55,165
(Screaming)

692
00:25:55,395 --> 00:25:56,935
The team will become stable...

693
00:25:56,935 --> 00:25:58,565
if there's someone I've worked with before.

694
00:25:58,765 --> 00:26:00,935
Will you work as a three-person team...

695
00:26:00,935 --> 00:26:03,005
or a four-person team?

696
00:26:03,175 --> 00:26:05,405
I will...

697
00:26:05,705 --> 00:26:08,745
not stop with forming my team.

698
00:26:08,745 --> 00:26:10,415
- Yes!
- One more!

699
00:26:10,415 --> 00:26:12,145
- That makes it more exciting.
- Yes!

700
00:26:12,345 --> 00:26:14,945
I could've stopped there as I was satisfied with the members.

701
00:26:14,945 --> 00:26:18,115
But I thought that there would be a better balance with another guy.

702
00:26:18,115 --> 00:26:20,825
Those older girls are too strong.

703
00:26:20,825 --> 00:26:21,855
I needed another member.

704
00:26:21,855 --> 00:26:23,255
Please!

705
00:26:24,755 --> 00:26:27,895
I hoped it was MIN JUN as I needed a storyteller.

706
00:26:27,925 --> 00:26:29,835
I really wanted to work with INGYOO.

707
00:26:30,295 --> 00:26:31,895
("Paradise")

708
00:26:32,105 --> 00:26:33,335
What a relief.

709
00:26:33,335 --> 00:26:34,735
(BABYZOO of "Born to Be Stars" is excluded.)

710
00:26:35,575 --> 00:26:37,105
I have no idea who it is.

711
00:26:37,105 --> 00:26:39,075
(Who is the owner of "Paradise" who will join INGYOO's team?)

712
00:26:39,945 --> 00:26:41,375
("Paradise" by JEONG MIN JUN)

713
00:26:41,645 --> 00:26:42,645
(Laughing)

714
00:26:42,775 --> 00:26:43,815
(Smiling brightly)

715
00:26:43,815 --> 00:26:45,885
I'm finally no longer the odd one out.

716
00:26:45,985 --> 00:26:47,945
Nice. I was satisfied with the team.

717
00:26:47,945 --> 00:26:49,585
We had the eyes of men and women.

718
00:26:49,585 --> 00:26:51,415
I believe we can share many different tastes.

719
00:26:51,485 --> 00:26:53,725
Right. The three of us are in a team.

720
00:26:53,725 --> 00:26:55,955
We had an accumulated collection of data.

721
00:26:55,955 --> 00:26:57,095
We have a good chance.

722
00:26:57,125 --> 00:26:58,555
There are two boomers in the team.

723
00:26:58,595 --> 00:27:00,295
"BABYZOO stuck in between the older ones."

724
00:27:00,295 --> 00:27:02,765
I will support them well as the youngest one.

725
00:27:02,865 --> 00:27:05,305
We have to go with a concept that's different from theirs.

726
00:27:05,305 --> 00:27:07,635
I hope we can look like a team...

727
00:27:07,635 --> 00:27:09,975
and make it look like one complete project.

728
00:27:09,975 --> 00:27:12,475
We seem to be the ones with more stability.

729
00:27:12,475 --> 00:27:14,075
The quality of the overall piece is important.

730
00:27:14,075 --> 00:27:17,045
That's the best for the individuals.

731
00:27:17,045 --> 00:27:18,915
I want us to work well as a team.

732
00:27:20,845 --> 00:27:22,115
This kid has no talent.

733
00:27:22,115 --> 00:27:23,115
The others are all great dancers.

734
00:27:23,585 --> 00:27:26,225
But what this kid had...

735
00:27:26,655 --> 00:27:27,825
was tenacity.

736
00:27:27,885 --> 00:27:31,155
Being consistent is also a great talent.

737
00:27:31,625 --> 00:27:33,965
The main character didn't have much talent.

738
00:27:33,965 --> 00:27:36,365
I wanted to throw a message...

739
00:27:36,365 --> 00:27:38,095
that being consistent is also a talent.

740
00:27:38,095 --> 00:27:40,165
This is one of the evaluation categories.

741
00:27:40,235 --> 00:27:41,835
"Did the star kid..."

742
00:27:41,835 --> 00:27:44,575
"show the potential of the next dance generation?"

743
00:27:44,635 --> 00:27:46,045
That topic...

744
00:27:46,045 --> 00:27:49,315
fits perfectly with this category.

745
00:27:49,315 --> 00:27:50,715
I wanted it to be a story that made sense...

746
00:27:50,715 --> 00:27:52,085
as it was about kids.

747
00:27:52,085 --> 00:27:54,145
As there was a slight connection with my concept,

748
00:27:54,145 --> 00:27:56,315
I thought I could express it very well.

749
00:27:56,385 --> 00:27:57,985
I want it to be bright.

750
00:27:58,055 --> 00:27:59,585
I want to match their eye level...

751
00:27:59,585 --> 00:28:02,095
and make something while hanging out with them.

752
00:28:02,255 --> 00:28:03,825
How does the secret playground sound?

753
00:28:03,895 --> 00:28:05,095
I have to be straightforward.

754
00:28:05,095 --> 00:28:06,625
I must be a strong leader.

755
00:28:06,695 --> 00:28:09,235
The tone that INGYOO had about what he was going to make...

756
00:28:09,235 --> 00:28:11,735
was similar to the concept I came up with.

757
00:28:11,735 --> 00:28:14,365
INGYOO's concept was distinct as his was chosen.

758
00:28:14,365 --> 00:28:16,535
I tried to listen to his opinion as much as possible.

759
00:28:16,535 --> 00:28:18,475
- Did you watch "Spider-Man?"
- The recent one?

760
00:28:18,475 --> 00:28:19,905
I think that's a good idea.

761
00:28:19,905 --> 00:28:21,475
The kids can wear masks.

762
00:28:21,545 --> 00:28:23,275
They'll become great dancers whenever they put on the masks.

763
00:28:23,275 --> 00:28:24,345
"Gosh!"

764
00:28:24,345 --> 00:28:26,085
(Like this)

765
00:28:26,145 --> 00:28:27,385
That's so cute.

766
00:28:27,385 --> 00:28:28,445
That's so cute!

767
00:28:28,445 --> 00:28:31,585
I liked the idea of the masks.

768
00:28:31,585 --> 00:28:33,955
They believe the talent comes from the masks.

769
00:28:33,985 --> 00:28:35,695
Right. That's how the story should go.

770
00:28:35,695 --> 00:28:36,995
But all they did was to take out what was inside.

771
00:28:36,995 --> 00:28:38,325
- But...
- Right.

772
00:28:38,395 --> 00:28:40,625
- The mask gave them the courage.
- Right.

773
00:28:40,625 --> 00:28:42,695
- It's like how you wear sunglasses.
- Right.

774
00:28:43,095 --> 00:28:46,435
The idea of shy kids discovering the masks.

775
00:28:46,435 --> 00:28:47,465
- Right.
- Right.

776
00:28:47,865 --> 00:28:49,135
The shy kids...

777
00:28:49,135 --> 00:28:51,035
discover masks and put them on.

778
00:28:51,035 --> 00:28:53,075
While fighting in a battle with confidence,

779
00:28:53,075 --> 00:28:54,245
the masks come off.

780
00:28:54,245 --> 00:28:56,515
The masks weren't the source of the superpowers.

781
00:28:56,645 --> 00:28:59,585
All they needed was the courage to bring out their talents.

782
00:28:59,645 --> 00:29:02,185
The penetrating message was really good.

783
00:29:02,185 --> 00:29:03,385
I earned a sense of certainty.

784
00:29:03,385 --> 00:29:04,985
- Hello.
- Hello.

785
00:29:04,985 --> 00:29:05,985
Hello.

786
00:29:05,985 --> 00:29:07,325
I want the music for Chapter 1 and Chapter 2...

787
00:29:07,325 --> 00:29:09,895
- to be quite aggressive.
- Right.

788
00:29:09,895 --> 00:29:11,725
It shouldn't just feel all happy.

789
00:29:11,725 --> 00:29:15,295
In Chapter Three, there should be a bridge that dies down.

790
00:29:15,365 --> 00:29:18,635
There should be a dramatic scene with a dance break.

791
00:29:18,805 --> 00:29:20,635
The piano sound will...

792
00:29:20,635 --> 00:29:21,635
- be in the background.
- Right.

793
00:29:21,705 --> 00:29:24,435
Whether it's Chapter 2 or Chapter 3,

794
00:29:24,435 --> 00:29:27,405
I wish for that sound to be in the background.

795
00:29:27,405 --> 00:29:28,645
- As for Chapter Three, - Okay.

796
00:29:28,645 --> 00:29:31,175
the song will build up with a lot more beats and choruses...

797
00:29:31,175 --> 00:29:32,745
along with the sessions.

798
00:29:32,745 --> 00:29:35,145
So ultimately, there are three chapters, right?

799
00:29:35,145 --> 00:29:38,185
Right. We want the song to be one complete song.

800
00:29:38,185 --> 00:29:39,355
One complete song...

801
00:29:39,355 --> 00:29:41,585
- instead of three different songs?
- Right.

802
00:29:41,585 --> 00:29:44,725
Things went smoothly.

803
