2380
01:28:21,928 --> 01:28:23,738
She's the next Kyoka.

2381
01:28:23,938 --> 01:28:25,398
I had only seen her video,

2382
01:28:25,398 --> 01:28:28,408
but just from that, I could tell she was a talented dancer.

2383
01:28:28,568 --> 01:28:30,738
I thought that if we recruited her, it would be game over.

2384
01:28:31,038 --> 01:28:33,308
Her sub-genre is acrobatics, and her main genre is hip-hop?

2385
01:28:33,308 --> 01:28:34,748
Acrobatics is her sub-genre?

2386
01:28:34,748 --> 01:28:36,218
Then there will be nothing she can't do.

2387
01:28:36,218 --> 01:28:38,548
I can't believe they let Yurichika and Qiuqiu battle.

2388
01:28:39,318 --> 01:28:42,148
If we fail to cast...

2389
01:28:42,148 --> 01:28:43,518
both A Zheng and Xunxun...

2390
01:28:43,618 --> 01:28:46,528
and have to pick our main character candidate...

2391
01:28:46,758 --> 01:28:48,658
- Yurichika?
- Yes, Yurichika.

2392
01:28:48,958 --> 01:28:49,958
That can be an option.

2393
01:28:49,958 --> 01:28:52,728
Yurichika already has a storyline written on her face.

2394
01:28:52,768 --> 01:28:53,798
I want Qiuqiu.

2395
01:28:53,798 --> 01:28:55,668
I think it'd be nice to have a B-boy.

2396
01:28:56,338 --> 01:28:59,338
The newly selected backup candidates for the main character...

2397
01:28:59,338 --> 01:29:01,238
were Qiuqiu and Yurichika.

2398
01:29:01,508 --> 01:29:03,278
Both Qiuqiu and Yurichika...

2399
01:29:03,278 --> 01:29:04,908
were dancers I coveted.

2400
01:29:05,138 --> 01:29:07,378
Do you have kid dancers you want as top priorities?

2401
01:29:07,548 --> 01:29:09,218
Yurichika and Honatsu.

2402
01:29:09,478 --> 01:29:11,448
It makes sense that MIN JUN wants her.

2403
01:29:11,448 --> 01:29:12,448
I know.

2404
01:29:12,448 --> 01:29:14,888
I really wanted to bring Yurichika in.

2405
01:29:14,888 --> 01:29:16,218
I wanted to cast her as Fear.

2406
01:29:16,218 --> 01:29:18,458
She acts all timid, but the second she dances, she changes...

2407
01:29:18,458 --> 01:29:19,758
and her side as a kid completely vanishes.

2408
01:29:20,028 --> 01:29:22,058
She was the character archetype I wanted to include.

2409
01:29:22,498 --> 01:29:25,158
If we fail to recruit the Third Bro,

2410
01:29:25,158 --> 01:29:26,798
there's someone who can fill in for the part.

2411
01:29:26,968 --> 01:29:28,328
- Qauqau? Qiuqiu?
- Right.

2412
01:29:28,368 --> 01:29:29,598
- Qauqau?
- Qauqau?

2413
01:29:29,968 --> 01:29:33,568
The trajectory of the synergy he can generate is enormous.

2414
01:29:33,568 --> 01:29:34,968
So I bet the 3-person team...

2415
01:29:34,968 --> 01:29:37,078
is having the same plan to recruit him.

2416
01:29:37,508 --> 01:29:40,148
A showdown between a B-boy and a hip-hop dancer.

2417
01:29:40,278 --> 01:29:41,908
Please introduce yourself.

2418
01:29:42,278 --> 01:29:44,018
I will blow you up.

2419
01:29:45,988 --> 01:29:48,048
(Cool!)

2420
01:29:48,048 --> 01:29:49,388
Qiuqiu is boiling over.

2421
01:29:49,658 --> 01:29:52,888
I just asked him for an introduction,

2422
01:29:52,888 --> 01:29:54,358
and he declared war.

2423
01:29:54,358 --> 01:29:55,898
Yurichika,

2424
01:29:55,898 --> 01:29:58,628
you should make a proper declaration of war too.

2425
01:29:58,628 --> 01:30:00,498
(Deep in thought)

2426
01:30:00,498 --> 01:30:02,128
(High expectations)

2427
01:30:02,538 --> 01:30:04,868
I will tear him up with everything I have.

2428
01:30:04,998 --> 01:30:06,568
(She's so cute.)

2429
01:30:06,768 --> 01:30:07,908
How adorable.

2430
01:30:07,908 --> 01:30:09,908
Dancers, please get ready for the battle.

2431
01:30:10,338 --> 01:30:11,378
(Chuckling)

2432
01:30:11,378 --> 01:30:12,408
What do I do?

2433
01:30:12,808 --> 01:30:14,508
Yurichika is going to show acrobatics, right?

2434
01:30:15,148 --> 01:30:16,918
(Taking it off again)

2435
01:30:17,278 --> 01:30:20,348
Look at those abs.

2436
01:30:20,548 --> 01:30:22,888
He's showing off so hard.

2437
01:30:22,888 --> 01:30:24,688
I think he's showing it off on purpose.

2438
01:30:25,388 --> 01:30:27,428
Go all out, Qiuqiu.

2439
01:30:27,688 --> 01:30:28,928
He's steeling his resolve.

2440
01:30:29,398 --> 01:30:30,658
World competition champion.

2441
01:30:30,658 --> 01:30:32,798
(The world champion's warm-up to assert dominance)

2442
01:30:34,368 --> 01:30:36,068
He's showing it off on purpose.

2443
01:30:36,138 --> 01:30:38,368
He won already. Yurichika is totally intimidated.

2444
01:30:38,768 --> 01:30:40,568
She's just stretching her legs.

2445
01:30:40,668 --> 01:30:43,178
In terms of genre, the two are different,

2446
01:30:43,408 --> 01:30:46,248
but we already have Niuniu for breaking.

2447
01:30:46,248 --> 01:30:48,448
If we want to showcase heavy breaking,

2448
01:30:48,448 --> 01:30:50,348
we'd need Qiuqiu.

2449
01:30:50,348 --> 01:30:52,918
Otherwise, I would love to have Yurichika.

2450
01:30:53,318 --> 01:30:56,158
I tried to watch closely so we could make the best use...

2451
01:30:56,158 --> 01:30:57,518
of their dancing and movement.

2452
01:30:57,518 --> 01:30:59,658
The battle between the two dancers begins now.

2453
01:30:59,658 --> 01:31:00,688
Ready!

2454
01:31:01,058 --> 01:31:02,798
- Fight!
- Let's go!

2455
01:31:02,928 --> 01:31:04,828
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2456
01:31:04,828 --> 01:31:06,068
Let's go, Qiuqiu!

2457
01:31:11,038 --> 01:31:12,468
Let's go, Qiuqiu!

2458
01:31:17,438 --> 01:31:19,048
His leg extension range is massive.

2459
01:31:19,548 --> 01:31:21,908
My goodness. Just how much did he practice that?

2460
01:31:21,908 --> 01:31:23,548
(Qiuqiu versus Yurichika)

2461
01:31:26,818 --> 01:31:28,148
Does this even make sense?

2462
01:31:28,288 --> 01:31:30,418
Keeping balance with such moves...

2463
01:31:30,418 --> 01:31:32,358
is an insane level of difficulty.

2464
01:31:32,358 --> 01:31:33,558
And in that position...

2465
01:31:34,028 --> 01:31:37,128
When you see something overwhelming, you become speechless.

2466
01:31:37,128 --> 01:31:39,528
Goosebumps break out, and every hair stands on end.

2467
01:31:39,898 --> 01:31:41,198
It was awe-inspiring.

2468
01:31:41,328 --> 01:31:43,968
How is this even possible? Isn't this insane?

2469
01:31:43,968 --> 01:31:44,998
My goodness.

2470
01:31:45,738 --> 01:31:47,168
(Qiuqiu versus Yurichika)

2471
01:31:47,168 --> 01:31:48,468
You're incredible.

2472
01:31:51,008 --> 01:31:52,678
(Amazed)

2473
01:31:54,078 --> 01:31:56,048
I wanted to recruit Qiuqiu.

2474
01:31:56,378 --> 01:31:57,518
This is insane.

2475
01:31:57,718 --> 01:31:59,488
- It's impossible.
- This is incredible.

2476
01:32:05,318 --> 01:32:06,858
I'm totally hooked. It's legendary.

2477
01:32:06,958 --> 01:32:08,058
How can kid B-boys...

2478
01:32:08,058 --> 01:32:10,698
execute skills at such an elite level?

2479
01:32:13,598 --> 01:32:14,768
He looks like Bruce Lee.

2480
01:32:17,168 --> 01:32:19,268
He was defying the laws of physics.

2481
01:32:19,908 --> 01:32:21,038
Come on!

2482
01:32:21,038 --> 01:32:22,808
I wanted to bring him onto our team so badly.

2483
01:32:22,808 --> 01:32:24,178
Two, one.

2484
01:32:24,178 --> 01:32:25,738
Switch! Yurichika!

2485
01:32:25,738 --> 01:32:27,148
He's not a kid.

2486
01:32:27,478 --> 01:32:29,008
He totally nailed it.

2487
01:32:29,418 --> 01:32:30,848
Two, one.

2488
01:32:30,848 --> 01:32:32,588
(Switch!)

2489
01:32:32,588 --> 01:32:34,448
Let's go!

2490
01:32:34,448 --> 01:32:36,758
(The second battler: Yurichika)

2491
01:32:38,788 --> 01:32:40,158
(Qiuqiu versus Yurichika)

2492
01:32:46,898 --> 01:32:49,168
Her sense of rhythm is incredible, as expected.

2493
01:32:52,638 --> 01:32:54,338
Her facial expressions were remarkably dynamic.

2494
01:32:54,568 --> 01:32:56,738
Let's go!

2495
01:33:00,878 --> 01:33:02,518
Look at that move. That's crazy.

2496
01:33:05,048 --> 01:33:06,848
I really want Yurichika.

2497
01:33:07,088 --> 01:33:09,048
She is definitely going to excel at everything.

2498
01:33:09,718 --> 01:33:10,858
She's amazing.

2499
01:33:12,318 --> 01:33:13,658
She's insanely good.

2500
01:33:13,658 --> 01:33:17,398
Watching a young girl dancer throw down hip-hop moves...

2501
01:33:17,528 --> 01:33:18,928
felt really unique.

2502
01:33:23,498 --> 01:33:26,638
(The music suddenly cuts off.)

2503
01:33:27,038 --> 01:33:30,208
(Yurichika keeps dancing without missing a beat.)

2504
01:33:30,208 --> 01:33:33,108
She was caught off guard...

2505
01:33:33,348 --> 01:33:34,578
by the edited audio track,

2506
01:33:34,578 --> 01:33:36,018
(She was caught off guard.)

2507
01:33:36,018 --> 01:33:38,048
but carried on seamlessly without showing it.

2508
01:33:38,048 --> 01:33:39,418
It was unbelievable.

2509
01:33:39,888 --> 01:33:41,488
She's so talented and seasoned.

2510
01:33:43,988 --> 01:33:46,728
Her musicality is incredible, and she is just insanely good.

2511
01:33:46,728 --> 01:33:49,398
- Hey!
- There you go!

2512
01:33:49,398 --> 01:33:51,058
Three, two, one.

2513
01:33:51,058 --> 01:33:54,828
The battle is over!

2514
01:33:54,998 --> 01:33:58,668
(The casting battle between Qiuqiu and Yurichika is over.)

2515
01:33:59,338 --> 01:34:00,468
That was amazing.

2516
01:34:00,638 --> 01:34:03,438
- They're just so good.
- It was unbelievable.

2517
01:34:03,678 --> 01:34:05,908
Wasn't Yurichika amazing at the beginning?

2518
01:34:05,908 --> 01:34:07,048
She looked so tough.

2519
01:34:07,378 --> 01:34:09,148
That was such a high-level battle.

2520
01:34:09,378 --> 01:34:11,448
Qiuqiu, you're so cool.

2521
01:34:11,678 --> 01:34:13,688
Wouldn't they choose Qiuqiu without question?

2522
01:34:14,088 --> 01:34:16,658
When it comes to breaking, Qiuqiu is the best.

2523
01:34:16,658 --> 01:34:19,228
- Right. He's the one.
- He's the final boss.

2524
01:34:19,388 --> 01:34:20,628
He is the king of B-boys here.

2525
01:34:20,628 --> 01:34:22,488
It makes sense why he swept world competitions.

2526
01:34:22,488 --> 01:34:23,998
It's unreal.

2527
01:34:24,398 --> 01:34:25,458
What do we do?

2528
01:34:25,458 --> 01:34:26,528
You want to pick this one?

2529
01:34:27,298 --> 01:34:29,098
- We should.
- What about this one?

2530
01:34:29,298 --> 01:34:30,668
Strategically speaking, I think we should pick this one.

2531
01:34:30,668 --> 01:34:31,998
- Because...
- I agree.

2532
01:34:31,998 --> 01:34:33,638
If we have her, we can make her the main character.

2533
01:34:33,638 --> 01:34:35,168
We can just use him for the big-impact move.

2534
01:34:35,168 --> 01:34:36,838
What if she goes to the other team?

2535
01:34:37,078 --> 01:34:38,478
- What if she leaves us?
- That's impossible.

2536
01:34:38,478 --> 01:34:39,508
What if she does?

2537
01:34:39,508 --> 01:34:40,608
It will never happen.

2538
01:34:40,608 --> 01:34:42,748
That scenario doesn't even exist.

2539
01:34:43,048 --> 01:34:45,448
- What do you think?
- They'll definitely pick this one.

2540
01:34:46,148 --> 01:34:48,548
(Predicting the 4-person team will choose Yurichika)

2541
01:34:48,788 --> 01:34:49,958
They immediately pointed to her.

2542
01:34:49,958 --> 01:34:51,918
(Kasper was watching everything.)

2543
01:34:51,918 --> 01:34:53,328
(Nodding his head)

2544
01:34:53,328 --> 01:34:55,388
Should we clash picks and get abandoned again?

2545
01:34:55,388 --> 01:34:56,458
Or...

2546
01:34:58,098 --> 01:35:00,268
(The men have grown accustomed to being abandoned.)

2547
01:35:00,268 --> 01:35:01,328
That's hilarious.

2548
01:35:01,768 --> 01:35:02,768
This is crazy.

2549
01:35:02,768 --> 01:35:05,068
I am prepared to die as many times as it takes.

2550
01:35:05,538 --> 01:35:07,668
- I don't mind it either.
- The thing is,

2551
01:35:07,838 --> 01:35:09,678
do we stack spectacle on top of spectacle?

2552
01:35:09,778 --> 01:35:11,238
Or do we go with pure choreography?

2553
01:35:11,378 --> 01:35:12,438
First off, both are so good.

2554
01:35:12,438 --> 01:35:15,248
Qiuqiu is just overwhelmingly good.

2555
01:35:15,748 --> 01:35:18,118
We could try some heavy breaking.

2556
01:35:18,348 --> 01:35:21,388
Already having secured Niuniu for breaking,

2557
01:35:21,488 --> 01:35:23,388
when considering whether we have enough scenes...

2558
01:35:23,388 --> 01:35:25,958
to maximize the synergy...

2559
01:35:25,958 --> 01:35:28,528
between Qiuqiu and Niuniu...

2560
01:35:28,758 --> 01:35:30,728
You know I'm using this element.

2561
01:35:31,128 --> 01:35:34,028
If they follow right after the bandage dance...

2562
01:35:34,028 --> 01:35:36,068
Doing it solo is quite typical.

2563
01:35:36,438 --> 01:35:38,268
We still need a main character.

2564
01:35:38,868 --> 01:35:42,068
I was solely fixated on the main character.

2565
01:35:42,368 --> 01:35:44,638
Could Qiuqiu actually pull off the main character?

2566
01:35:44,978 --> 01:35:46,978
(Who did the two teams choose?)

2567
01:35:47,148 --> 01:35:49,148
Please reveal the casting board.

2568
01:35:50,148 --> 01:35:52,078
(Both teams chose Yurichika.)

2569
01:35:53,788 --> 01:35:57,058
Our choices clashed again, as expected.

2570
01:35:57,388 --> 01:35:58,718
We might not...

2571
01:35:59,288 --> 01:36:00,758
be able to recruit her.

2572
01:36:00,758 --> 01:36:03,858
(It overlapped again.)

2573
01:36:04,158 --> 01:36:06,198
I guess they went with a similar strategy to ours.

2574
01:36:08,128 --> 01:36:10,198
To me, Qiuqiu was just on a different level.

2575
01:36:10,198 --> 01:36:11,738
I completely fell in love with him.

2576
01:36:11,738 --> 01:36:14,708
Based purely on the battle, it had to be Qiuqiu.

2577
01:36:14,938 --> 01:36:16,208
But the dilemma was that...

2578
01:36:16,478 --> 01:36:19,648
we already had a breaking dancer on our team.

2579
01:36:19,908 --> 01:36:21,578
I wasn't sure if casting another breaker was the right move.

2580
01:36:21,578 --> 01:36:23,648
So we decided to cast a hip-hop dancer...

2581
01:36:23,648 --> 01:36:25,718
since we were missing hip-hop as a genre.

2582
01:36:25,848 --> 01:36:27,588
So we chose Yurichika.

2583
01:36:28,018 --> 01:36:29,688
I'm getting the feeling that...

2584
01:36:29,688 --> 01:36:31,388
we could consider him to take the lead role.

2585
01:36:32,188 --> 01:36:33,258
- I was pushing for him.
- Yes.

2586
01:36:33,258 --> 01:36:35,188
Right. That's what I remember.

2587
01:36:35,328 --> 01:36:36,898
You wanted Yurichika.

2588
01:36:37,098 --> 01:36:39,798
- She has an androgynous charm.
- Yes.

2589
01:36:39,798 --> 01:36:41,528
I mean, she's got that look.

2590
01:36:41,528 --> 01:36:42,998
- Isn't she perfect in films?
- Yes, she is.

2591
01:36:42,998 --> 01:36:44,498
She's got that look.

2592
01:36:44,738 --> 01:36:46,908
I thought we needed a dancer...

2593
01:36:46,908 --> 01:36:49,038
with expressive eyes and strong facial expressions.

2594
01:36:49,068 --> 01:36:51,378
Considering my approach, I checked all the boxes...

2595
01:36:51,378 --> 01:36:53,008
when she was battling...

2596
01:36:53,008 --> 01:36:55,108
and dancing.

2597
01:36:55,148 --> 01:36:57,478
I had this feeling that she could take the lead role.

2598
01:36:57,478 --> 01:36:59,948
(Which team will she pick?)

2599
01:37:00,148 --> 01:37:02,518
I really want Yurichika on my team.

2600
01:37:03,018 --> 01:37:05,718
Why is she walking toward right like the others?

2601
01:37:06,328 --> 01:37:08,488
She would pick us, wouldn't she?

2602
01:37:08,958 --> 01:37:10,398
Please.

2603
01:37:12,298 --> 01:37:14,528
(Yurichika picks the 3-person team.)

2604
01:37:14,528 --> 01:37:16,468
- No way!
- My gosh.

2605
01:37:16,468 --> 01:37:18,768
(Shocked)

2606
01:37:18,868 --> 01:37:20,768
(I can't believe this!)

2607
01:37:20,808 --> 01:37:22,568
(At last!)

2608
01:37:22,568 --> 01:37:24,708
(No way!)

2609
01:37:24,978 --> 01:37:27,308
She went to the team with Mr. Koo Young, Mr. Kasper,

2610
01:37:27,448 --> 01:37:29,718
and Uncle BABYZOO.

2611
01:37:29,748 --> 01:37:30,978
I was heartbroken.

2612
01:37:31,148 --> 01:37:33,348
- I'm so touched.
- Thank you.

2613
01:37:33,548 --> 01:37:36,358
- Yurichika!
- Thank you.

2614
01:37:36,888 --> 01:37:41,828
I liked BABYZOO, so I chose the three-person team.

2615
01:37:43,558 --> 01:37:45,498
Thank you so much for picking us.

2616
01:37:45,498 --> 01:37:49,098
To us, Yurichika is like a deity.

2617
01:37:49,228 --> 01:37:52,698
When we tried to find the right dancer to take the lead role,

2618
01:37:52,698 --> 01:37:53,808
we came up empty.

2619
01:37:53,808 --> 01:37:55,938
Then she came to save us.

2620
01:37:55,938 --> 01:37:57,538
She really is a lifesaver.

2621
01:37:57,638 --> 01:37:59,608
- Qiuqiu.
- Qiuqiu.

2622
01:37:59,608 --> 01:38:00,708
You're number one.

2623
01:38:00,708 --> 01:38:03,478
(Qiuqiu will join the 4-person team.)

2624
01:38:03,478 --> 01:38:05,178
Qiuqiu. Let's go.

2625
01:38:05,578 --> 01:38:06,788
This is interesting.

2626
01:38:06,988 --> 01:38:08,748
- That was crazy.
- What a surprise.

2627
01:38:08,748 --> 01:38:10,188
We're good now. We can afford to lose here on out.

2628
01:38:10,188 --> 01:38:11,318
(Just happy)

2629
01:38:11,388 --> 01:38:13,428
It feels great to be chosen.

2630
01:38:14,158 --> 01:38:15,528
I mean it.

2631
01:38:15,858 --> 01:38:17,098
I was really surprised.

2632
01:38:17,098 --> 01:38:18,158
(It feels this good?)

2633
01:38:18,158 --> 01:38:19,258
How do you feel now?

2634
01:38:19,258 --> 01:38:20,998
My heart sank for a moment.

2635
01:38:21,268 --> 01:38:23,098
Your heart sank, right? Boom.

2636
01:38:23,098 --> 01:38:24,868
It's been like that for us the whole time.

2637
01:38:26,168 --> 01:38:28,568
Only one casting battle remains now.

2638
01:38:28,868 --> 01:38:30,308
It's Rikka versus Sun Manhang.

2639
01:38:30,938 --> 01:38:32,408
It was the last battle.

2640
01:38:32,638 --> 01:38:35,308
I tried to figure out what to look for in this battle.

2641
01:38:35,578 --> 01:38:38,548
Rikka specializes in jazz-focused choreography.

2642
01:38:38,948 --> 01:38:41,318
Sun Manhang specializes in hip-hop-focused choreography.

2643
01:38:42,088 --> 01:38:43,688
Their main genres are different.

2644
01:38:43,688 --> 01:38:45,758
I'm wondering what kind of energy they'll show us.

2645
01:38:45,818 --> 01:38:47,688
- Which one should we pick?
- We were trying to figure that out.

2646
01:38:47,758 --> 01:38:50,198
We were chosen by the dancers we wanted.

2647
01:38:50,428 --> 01:38:52,528
It'd be nice to get a dancer for a position we're missing.

2648
01:38:52,798 --> 01:38:54,828
Ready, fight.

2649
01:38:54,828 --> 01:38:55,898
Let's go!

2650
01:38:56,368 --> 01:38:58,868
- Gosh.
- She was at the top of my list.

2651
01:38:58,868 --> 01:39:00,008
Let's go, Rikka!

2652
01:39:03,578 --> 01:39:04,678
(Captivated)

2653
01:39:04,678 --> 01:39:06,578
I love it.

2654
01:39:08,848 --> 01:39:10,678
She's super talented.

2655
01:39:11,918 --> 01:39:12,918
Switch.

2656
01:39:13,748 --> 01:39:15,488
(Sun Manhang is next.)

2657
01:39:15,618 --> 01:39:16,888
He's having fun.

2658
01:39:16,888 --> 01:39:17,988
(Nervous)

2659
01:39:19,188 --> 01:39:20,188
(Impressed)

2660
01:39:21,228 --> 01:39:22,958
- He's good!
- He's great.

2661
01:39:23,098 --> 01:39:24,158
- He's good.
- What?

2662
01:39:24,158 --> 01:39:25,728
I had no idea he was that good.

2663
01:39:26,598 --> 01:39:28,098
He danced perfectly on the beat.

2664
01:39:28,428 --> 01:39:29,868
Hey, he's so good.

2665
01:39:29,868 --> 01:39:31,568
He was in complete control.

2666
01:39:34,168 --> 01:39:36,508
(Bobbing his head)

2667
01:39:36,538 --> 01:39:38,338
(That's some crazy confidence.)

2668
01:39:38,908 --> 01:39:40,378
Battle over.

2669
01:39:41,178 --> 01:39:43,518
I was impressed by his dancing.

2670
01:39:43,978 --> 01:39:46,248
Actually, we weren't considering casting...

2671
01:39:46,248 --> 01:39:47,788
Sun Manhang at first.

2672
01:39:48,248 --> 01:39:51,188
As soon as I saw him dance, he won me over.

2673
01:39:51,318 --> 01:39:54,928
We absolutely needed him for our film.

2674
01:39:55,188 --> 01:39:57,998
I thought he'd be great for bringing that extra flavor to our film.

2675
01:39:58,458 --> 01:40:00,198
(Their decisions overlapped even to the last casting battle.)

2676
01:40:01,498 --> 01:40:02,598
This is legendary.

2677
01:40:02,728 --> 01:40:04,398
Please join our team.

2678
01:40:04,668 --> 01:40:06,198
Which team...

2679
01:40:06,198 --> 01:40:08,738
will he choose?

2680
01:40:10,078 --> 01:40:11,108
Okay.

2681
01:40:11,108 --> 01:40:12,708
(Should I go to them or not?)

2682
01:40:13,048 --> 01:40:14,408
Please.

2683
01:40:15,678 --> 01:40:16,748
He's playful.

2684
01:40:16,918 --> 01:40:18,318
We need him on our team.

2685
01:40:18,548 --> 01:40:20,748
(Which team will this playful dancer pick?)

2686
01:40:22,248 --> 01:40:23,788
(He picks the 4-person team.)

2687
01:40:23,788 --> 01:40:25,958
- Okay. He chose...
- Thank you.

2688
01:40:25,958 --> 01:40:27,158
the four-person team.

2689
01:40:27,188 --> 01:40:29,488
(Rikka picks the 3-person team.)

2690
01:40:29,488 --> 01:40:30,928
Rikka is great too.

2691
01:40:30,928 --> 01:40:33,298
I'm sure she'll shine more on our team.

2692
01:40:33,328 --> 01:40:35,098
It's a pity, but what could I do?

2693
01:40:35,098 --> 01:40:37,498
We haven't tried anything with them yet.

2694
01:40:37,568 --> 01:40:38,838
We must make it work no matter what.

2695
01:40:38,838 --> 01:40:40,338
I'll do my best.

2696
01:40:40,508 --> 01:40:42,308
"Super Kids Direct Mission, Judges' Evaluation."

2697
01:40:42,368 --> 01:40:44,708
"Stay in your Directors' Room."

2698
01:40:44,978 --> 01:40:46,678
(What's going on?)

2699
01:40:47,108 --> 01:40:48,108
(They're bringing in chairs?)

2700
01:40:48,108 --> 01:40:49,648
My gosh. Come on. This is crazy.

2701
01:40:49,648 --> 01:40:51,848
I'm going to watch the judges watch it?

2702
01:40:51,848 --> 01:40:53,788
(With the glass wall between us?)

2703
01:40:53,888 --> 01:40:54,918
(Right before my eyes?)

2704
01:40:54,918 --> 01:40:56,358
(Screaming)

2705
01:40:56,358 --> 01:40:57,518
(Knocked out)

2706
01:40:57,588 --> 01:41:01,358
(The judges start evaluating with everyone watching.)

2707
01:41:01,388 --> 01:41:02,828
(It worked!)

2708
01:41:02,828 --> 01:41:05,658
(Wild applause from the judges)

2709
01:41:05,658 --> 01:41:06,768
(We got it. That's the reaction.)

2710
01:41:06,768 --> 01:41:07,798
(Nice!)

2711
01:41:07,798 --> 01:41:09,198
(So cute!)

2712
01:41:09,328 --> 01:41:11,768
Four of the seven directors...

2713
01:41:11,868 --> 01:41:14,868
will head to Last Stage: 24H.

2714
01:41:15,108 --> 01:41:16,478
Four of the seven directors?

2715
01:41:16,908 --> 01:41:18,278
(This is super cool.)

2716
01:41:18,278 --> 01:41:20,048
(Who's that?)

2717
01:41:20,048 --> 01:41:24,018
(Revealing the kids' film that drove the judges mad)

2718
01:41:24,418 --> 01:41:25,418
Is that you?

2719
01:41:25,648 --> 01:41:26,818
(15 days left until the shoot of the film)

2720
01:41:26,818 --> 01:41:28,618
(The day of the production meeting)

2721
01:41:30,588 --> 01:41:32,788
The film director is here.

2722
01:41:32,788 --> 01:41:34,828
We'll start the meeting now.

2723
01:41:35,388 --> 01:41:38,498
Sung Jin has a lot of experience with filming dance videos.

2724
01:41:38,498 --> 01:41:39,998
(Jennie's performance video)

2725
01:41:39,998 --> 01:41:42,128
He also worked a lot with INGYOO and Simeez.

2726
01:41:42,128 --> 01:41:43,738
I've worked with him once before.

2727
01:41:44,138 --> 01:41:45,368
I'm in charge of Chapter One.

2728
01:41:45,368 --> 01:41:47,538
The intro will be included in Chapter One.

2729
01:41:47,538 --> 01:41:49,778
She's going to school like any other day.

2730
01:41:50,138 --> 01:41:53,308
Then she finds a door that leads to a different world.

2731
01:41:53,448 --> 01:41:54,878
- Four or five dancers?
- So she can't be confident?

2732
01:41:54,878 --> 01:41:56,878
- Exactly. A group of timid kids.
- Right. They'd be like this.

2733
01:41:57,018 --> 01:41:59,448
"I want to be like them." That's the idea.

2734
01:41:59,748 --> 01:42:01,188
Timid dancers...

2735
01:42:01,188 --> 01:42:02,618
find masks.

2736
01:42:02,618 --> 01:42:03,788
- When they put the masks on...
- It happens here.

2737
01:42:03,888 --> 01:42:05,958
Oh, my. They turn into Super Kids.

2738
01:42:06,018 --> 01:42:08,628
It's like they're under a spell. "Hey, you try it on too."

2739
01:42:08,628 --> 01:42:10,558
The plot will heighten in my chapter.

2740
01:42:10,558 --> 01:42:12,458
There will be a battle in my chapter.

2741
01:42:12,598 --> 01:42:14,868
This is the most powerful part of the film.

2742
01:42:14,868 --> 01:42:17,168
Then the mask comes off and gets destroyed.

2743
01:42:17,198 --> 01:42:18,968
When it comes off, it'd be like... "I'm doomed."

2744
01:42:19,068 --> 01:42:20,708
"What if I can't dance?"

2745
01:42:20,708 --> 01:42:22,738
The masks didn't make them good dancers. The truth is,

2746
01:42:22,738 --> 01:42:24,478
the masks gave them courage.

2747
01:42:24,738 --> 01:42:27,048
After building up the plot, there will be a dance break.

2748
01:42:27,048 --> 01:42:28,378
- Everyone will dance together.
- Yes.

2749
01:42:28,408 --> 01:42:30,618
I'm in charge of Chapter Four.

2750
01:42:30,848 --> 01:42:33,918
When they're all running out, we're going to bring in the rain.

2751
01:42:34,048 --> 01:42:36,688
The energy level will build up throughout the film.

2752
01:42:36,818 --> 01:42:38,558
Then it will just blow up with the rain.

2753
01:42:38,788 --> 01:42:41,928
They're going to dance in the rain. After that...

2754
01:42:41,988 --> 01:42:43,028
The audience sees that...

2755
01:42:43,028 --> 01:42:44,658
we were the ones who put the masks there.

2756
01:42:44,658 --> 01:42:46,628
We're going to place the masks somewhere else again.

2757
01:42:46,628 --> 01:42:48,028
- For the next generation.
- Yes.

2758
01:42:48,498 --> 01:42:49,838
It might come across as light.

2759
01:42:50,138 --> 01:42:52,268
But kids should keep things light, not heavy.

2760
01:42:52,398 --> 01:42:54,068
We can't make this difficult.

2761
01:42:54,068 --> 01:42:55,068
(On the same day, the 3-person team has a production meeting too.)

2762
01:42:55,068 --> 01:42:57,008
(Director Back Koo Young is abroad on a business trip.)

2763
01:42:57,108 --> 01:43:00,178
This isn't just a performance film. We need a story.

2764
01:43:01,308 --> 01:43:02,548
Would we be able to film it in one day?

2765
01:43:02,748 --> 01:43:03,748
That's my biggest concern.

2766
01:43:04,778 --> 01:43:07,118
(The music video of BLACKPINK's "GO")

2767
01:43:07,448 --> 01:43:09,088
She did the music video of aespa's "Armageddon."

2768
01:43:10,018 --> 01:43:12,188
She also worked with ALLDAY PROJECT.

2769
01:43:12,388 --> 01:43:15,428
She has to be the most famous director for dance films.

2770
01:43:15,428 --> 01:43:17,198
Jun Hui had her phone number.

2771
01:43:17,428 --> 01:43:19,698
I know Director Yoon Seung Rim.

2772
01:43:19,698 --> 01:43:22,098
- Who?
- I know Director Seung Rim.

2773
01:43:22,398 --> 01:43:24,638
- We'd like to work with you.
- Yes.

2774
01:43:24,668 --> 01:43:27,068
We already came up with the story.

2775
01:43:27,208 --> 01:43:29,368
So we called her right away.

2776
01:43:29,568 --> 01:43:32,078
At first, she said no. So Tae Woo called her.

2777
01:43:32,178 --> 01:43:33,648
It was like trying to win over Zhuge Liang...

2778
01:43:33,748 --> 01:43:35,108
by persuading her repeatedly.

2779
01:43:35,208 --> 01:43:37,118
But we managed to get her on our team,

2780
01:43:37,118 --> 01:43:38,778
and we can't wait to work with her.

2781
01:43:38,978 --> 01:43:41,388
I think the quality of our film will be much higher...

2782
01:43:41,388 --> 01:43:42,918
than theirs.

2783
01:43:43,088 --> 01:43:45,418
In the story we're picturing,

2784
01:43:45,418 --> 01:43:47,428
they have to face two moments of despair.

2785
01:43:47,428 --> 01:43:48,928
- Okay.
- The first moment will be...

2786
01:43:48,928 --> 01:43:50,428
after the battle.

2787
01:43:50,528 --> 01:43:52,498
The second moment will be after getting injured.

2788
01:43:52,628 --> 01:43:54,868
My chapter is all about setting up the storyline.

2789
01:43:54,868 --> 01:43:57,738
When she faces another crisis, she'll be in despair.

2790
01:43:57,798 --> 01:44:00,708
With the support of her friends, she'll recover from her injury.

2791
01:44:01,068 --> 01:44:03,138
Then she'll unwrap the bandage,

2792
01:44:03,138 --> 01:44:05,738
dance with the bandage, and throw it away.

2793
01:44:05,908 --> 01:44:08,278
She and her friends will become one.

2794
01:44:08,478 --> 01:44:10,478
My chapter will play a critical role in leading the story...

2795
01:44:10,478 --> 01:44:12,148
into the third chapter.

2796
01:44:12,348 --> 01:44:14,918
My chapter might be slightly iffy.

2797
01:44:14,988 --> 01:44:16,988
Toward the end, it's mostly dancing.

2798
01:44:16,988 --> 01:44:19,458
The storyline mainly comes from the beginning of the film.

2799
01:44:19,618 --> 01:44:21,428
It's not just a group scene.

2800
01:44:21,428 --> 01:44:23,128
It's not a mega crew performance.

2801
01:44:23,398 --> 01:44:26,098
If the group dance is only highlighted in my chapter,

2802
01:44:26,158 --> 01:44:28,998
it won't leave a strong impression compared to the 1st 2 chapters.

2803
01:44:28,998 --> 01:44:31,368
I need to add more story elements to my chapter.

2804
01:44:31,538 --> 01:44:33,268
I do have an idea.

2805
01:44:33,368 --> 01:44:36,578
Do you know why water bottles are important to battlers?

2806
01:44:36,678 --> 01:44:38,178
That decides who goes first.

2807
01:44:38,178 --> 01:44:40,808
Whoever goes first has to dance right away without the chance...

2808
01:44:40,808 --> 01:44:41,878
to listen to the song.

2809
01:44:41,978 --> 01:44:43,818
Because the bottle decides who goes first,

2810
01:44:43,818 --> 01:44:46,848
the bottle cap is super important.

2811
01:44:47,188 --> 01:44:48,988
We could try to convey...

2812
01:44:48,988 --> 01:44:51,958
that it doesn't matter anymore in the end.

2813
01:44:51,958 --> 01:44:53,928
- I see.
- Going 1st or 2nd...

2814
01:44:53,928 --> 01:44:55,288
Or having the chance to listen to the song...

2815
01:44:55,528 --> 01:44:58,158
They don't need that kind of benefit to win the battles.

2816
01:44:58,198 --> 01:45:00,698
In the end, we'll be evaluated individually.

2817
01:45:00,798 --> 01:45:03,998
Now, it's an individual mission under the name of a team mission.

2818
01:45:04,068 --> 01:45:05,298
All that matters now is this pretense.

2819
01:45:05,368 --> 01:45:07,738
It's very important to figure out a way...

2820
01:45:07,738 --> 01:45:08,908
to make my chapter shine.

2821
01:45:09,638 --> 01:45:11,178
We're at the location.

2822
01:45:11,208 --> 01:45:12,478
Yaho.

2823
01:45:12,708 --> 01:45:14,448
- Yaho.
- Dangjin, yaho.

2824
01:45:14,648 --> 01:45:16,478
It used to be a prayer center. Why does it look so pretty?

2825
01:45:16,578 --> 01:45:17,848
It has a nice vibe to it. I like it.

2826
01:45:18,278 --> 01:45:20,088
As for the film location we wanted,

2827
01:45:20,148 --> 01:45:21,748
considering the development of the plot,

2828
01:45:21,748 --> 01:45:24,558
it couldn't be just bright or dark.

2829
01:45:24,618 --> 01:45:27,028
It had to be bright, but dark at the same time.

2830
01:45:27,028 --> 01:45:28,488
It needed cool, yet warm vibes.

2831
01:45:28,588 --> 01:45:30,558
Chapter Four needs that childlike mood.

2832
01:45:30,558 --> 01:45:31,858
It has to look...

2833
01:45:31,858 --> 01:45:34,168
youthful and bright in an open area. It has to look lively.

2834
01:45:34,168 --> 01:45:36,398
In the last chapter, they're going to be on a big field.

2835
01:45:36,398 --> 01:45:38,168
And they'll bond through dancing.

2836
01:45:38,368 --> 01:45:39,568
Everything will pay off then.

2837
01:45:39,638 --> 01:45:40,908
It will be better up there.

2838
01:45:41,238 --> 01:45:42,408
(It's full of lively vibes.)

2839
01:45:42,408 --> 01:45:44,478
We can make use of everything here.

2840
01:45:44,478 --> 01:45:46,778
Filming the second chapter here sounds good too.

2841
01:45:47,008 --> 01:45:48,378
Then we can't film the last chapter here.

2842
01:45:48,478 --> 01:45:49,808
If this is the angle for the last chapter,

2843
01:45:49,808 --> 01:45:51,148
- we could do this for my chapter.
- But...

2844
01:45:51,148 --> 01:45:52,578
- We need a wide-angle shot.
- Yes.

2845
01:45:52,578 --> 01:45:54,248
The dancers will be up there too.

2846
01:45:54,688 --> 01:45:56,588
- This would work for my chapter.
- But not the second chapter.

2847
01:45:56,588 --> 01:45:57,588
If we use this spot for the fourth chapter,

2848
01:45:57,588 --> 01:45:58,618
we don't have an option for the second chapter.

2849
01:45:58,688 --> 01:46:01,158
Would that be weird? The spot we saw from the entrance?

2850
01:46:01,258 --> 01:46:02,388
That doesn't look that interesting.

2851
01:46:03,528 --> 01:46:04,598
It didn't go smoothly.

2852
01:46:04,658 --> 01:46:07,368
We had different opinions for each chapter.

2853
01:46:07,368 --> 01:46:09,938
That was the obstacle we had.

2854
01:46:10,398 --> 01:46:12,498
I'm afraid that this might not be the best spot for our film.

2855
01:46:12,668 --> 01:46:15,508
It was too dark and looked too humble.

2856
01:46:15,568 --> 01:46:16,938
We need to keep...

2857
01:46:16,938 --> 01:46:19,138
exploring more locations until we're satisfied.

2858
01:46:20,608 --> 01:46:22,108
(The 4-person team decided on their final location.)

2859
01:46:22,348 --> 01:46:24,378
It's not a place you'd find in real life.

2860
01:46:24,418 --> 01:46:26,248
It reminds me of "Alice in Wonderland."

2861
01:46:26,788 --> 01:46:28,388
I was shocked by the scale of it.

2862
01:46:28,388 --> 01:46:30,088
It was exactly what we were looking for.

2863
01:46:30,088 --> 01:46:32,558
We'd be able to film a lot of interesting scenes.

2864
01:46:33,218 --> 01:46:34,328
(The last production meeting for the 3-person team)

2865
01:46:34,558 --> 01:46:36,458
All three of our chapters look cool.

2866
01:46:36,458 --> 01:46:37,998
Our overall plot is amazing.

2867
01:46:38,058 --> 01:46:40,568
You never know. They might start crying all of a sudden.

2868
01:46:40,568 --> 01:46:42,428
- They're great dancers.
- Yes.

2869
01:46:42,428 --> 01:46:43,768
But they're still kids.

2870
01:46:43,868 --> 01:46:45,238
- It might not look real or cool.
- Right.

2871
01:46:45,238 --> 01:46:47,238
That did cross my mind.

2872
01:46:47,238 --> 01:46:48,638
The girl who we wanted for the lead role...

2873
01:46:48,638 --> 01:46:50,078
She said she couldn't do it because of the pressure.

2874
01:46:50,078 --> 01:46:51,438
She wanted someone else to take the role.

2875
01:46:52,178 --> 01:46:55,748
We decided that we wanted Yurichika for the lead role.

2876
01:46:55,908 --> 01:46:57,148
Yurichika.

2877
01:46:57,148 --> 01:46:58,978
Have you ever tried acting before?

2878
01:46:58,978 --> 01:47:00,788
I was in second grade.

2879
01:47:00,888 --> 01:47:03,818
I performed in a musical.

2880
01:47:03,818 --> 01:47:05,388
So I tried acting before.

2881
01:47:05,418 --> 01:47:08,788
We might need you to portray different kinds of emotions.

2882
01:47:08,788 --> 01:47:10,158
Do you think you can do it?

2883
01:47:10,228 --> 01:47:11,258
Yes.

2884
01:47:12,228 --> 01:47:13,628
I love your smile.

2885
01:47:13,628 --> 01:47:15,198
- She has a pure and innocent smile.
- Yes.

2886
01:47:15,428 --> 01:47:16,598
She's got it all.

2887
01:47:16,868 --> 01:47:17,968
Could we ask her...

2888
01:47:17,968 --> 01:47:19,898
to act angry?

2889
01:47:19,968 --> 01:47:21,668
(She starts acting on the spot.)

2890
01:47:21,668 --> 01:47:22,708
(Winning over the uncles already)

2891
01:47:22,708 --> 01:47:23,738
(Frowning fiercely)

2892
01:47:23,738 --> 01:47:24,838
(She's perfect to take the lead role.)

2893
01:47:24,938 --> 01:47:26,238
In my chapter,

2894
01:47:26,238 --> 01:47:28,978
she has to convey to the audience she's in despair.

2895
01:47:29,008 --> 01:47:31,718
Facial expressions are going to play an important role.

2896
01:47:31,778 --> 01:47:34,148
I'd like to explain the story.

2897
01:47:34,248 --> 01:47:35,288
(Explain the story?)

2898
01:47:35,348 --> 01:47:38,118
You'll be sitting at a table at the beginning of the story.

2899
01:47:38,118 --> 01:47:42,688
Because you're angry, you're going to break the table leg.

2900
01:47:43,798 --> 01:47:46,528
In the end, you and your friends...

2901
01:47:46,798 --> 01:47:48,768
will happily dance together.

2902
01:47:50,138 --> 01:47:51,268
That's the story.

2903
01:47:52,368 --> 01:47:53,468
What's wrong?

2904
01:47:55,068 --> 01:47:56,108
Are you all right?

2905
01:47:57,678 --> 01:47:58,738
Are you okay?

2906
01:47:59,778 --> 01:48:00,878
Was I too scary?

2907
01:48:03,718 --> 01:48:06,048
I've done musicals.

2908
01:48:06,048 --> 01:48:08,948
But I've never done plays.

2909
01:48:09,618 --> 01:48:11,758
I've never done real acting.

2910
01:48:13,218 --> 01:48:14,728
She cried,

2911
01:48:14,728 --> 01:48:15,888
so I was worried about her.

2912
01:48:16,258 --> 01:48:18,928
The pressure was too much for me.

2913
01:48:19,898 --> 01:48:21,028
You needed to start practicing soon.

2914
01:48:21,028 --> 01:48:22,968
Didn't you feel like you didn't have enough time?

2915
01:48:22,968 --> 01:48:24,298
That wasn't important.

2916
01:48:24,298 --> 01:48:25,368
She was crying.

2917
01:48:25,438 --> 01:48:27,068
I told her it was okay.

2918
01:48:27,238 --> 01:48:28,738
I told her she could just learn the moves.

2919
01:48:28,738 --> 01:48:29,938
Great. At first...

2920
01:48:30,008 --> 01:48:31,908
I asked her if she didn't mind learning the choreography.

2921
01:48:31,908 --> 01:48:34,608
(She calmed down little by little while learning the choreography.)

2922
01:48:34,908 --> 01:48:37,378
I told her to think about it if the role was too much for her...

2923
01:48:37,378 --> 01:48:39,278
and let me know what she wanted to do later.

2924
01:48:39,918 --> 01:48:42,148
(Yurichika decided to try out for the main character.)

2925
01:48:42,188 --> 01:48:45,858
At first, it was a lot of pressure.

2926
01:48:45,858 --> 01:48:48,428
But now, I'm quite confident.

2927
01:48:49,158 --> 01:48:50,328
That's interesting.

2928
01:48:50,328 --> 01:48:52,398
I thought she'd be happy.

2929
01:48:52,398 --> 01:48:54,028
But it was overwhelming for her.

2930
01:48:54,068 --> 01:48:57,598
She must've felt a lot of pressure because she had to lead...

2931
01:48:57,668 --> 01:48:59,068
the story with her acting.

2932
01:48:59,068 --> 01:49:00,568
I thought we should...

2933
01:49:00,568 --> 01:49:02,768
try harder to communicate with her.

2934
01:49:02,768 --> 01:49:03,908
That crossed my mind.

2935
01:49:03,908 --> 01:49:05,438
My top priority is that...

2936
01:49:05,438 --> 01:49:07,408
these kids can complete the shoot without getting hurt.

2937
01:49:07,408 --> 01:49:09,178
I'll do my best...

2938
01:49:09,178 --> 01:49:10,948
and take care of them as their director.

2939
01:49:11,948 --> 01:49:13,418
All right. Let's try this.

2940
01:49:13,448 --> 01:49:15,418
(The 3-person team starts practicing for Chapter 3 in earnest.)

2941
01:49:15,418 --> 01:49:17,418
(Today's teacher, Kasper)

2942
01:49:17,718 --> 01:49:18,888
(When he jumps, )

2943
01:49:18,988 --> 01:49:20,388
(the kids jump too.)

2944
01:49:20,388 --> 01:49:21,558
(Papa Koo also jumps.)

2945
01:49:21,558 --> 01:49:24,258
To make this look hip,

2946
01:49:24,258 --> 01:49:26,098
we're going to try it with a jacket.

2947
01:49:26,558 --> 01:49:29,068
(Trying on the padded jacket to make it look hip)

2948
01:49:29,168 --> 01:49:30,198
What do you think?

2949
01:49:30,198 --> 01:49:31,198
It looks great.

2950
01:49:31,198 --> 01:49:32,198
Really?

2951
01:49:32,198 --> 01:49:33,268
It does look great.

2952
01:49:33,298 --> 01:49:35,768
(Koo Young also puts on the jacket.)

2953
01:49:35,968 --> 01:49:37,008
(He's getting excited.)

2954
01:49:37,008 --> 01:49:38,108
(Papa Koo is especially swift today.)

2955
01:49:38,778 --> 01:49:39,908
What was that?

2956
01:49:39,908 --> 01:49:41,348
I just almost slipped.

2957
01:49:41,608 --> 01:49:42,648
(Chuckling)

2958
01:49:42,648 --> 01:49:44,478
(I want to try it too.)

2959
01:49:44,478 --> 01:49:45,778
(He's funny.)

2960
01:49:45,778 --> 01:49:47,118
Ever since you put on the jacket,

2961
01:49:47,118 --> 01:49:48,218
you suddenly...

2962
01:49:48,218 --> 01:49:49,648
- look tough.
- My facial expression...

2963
01:49:49,648 --> 01:49:51,558
with this jacket...

2964
01:49:51,558 --> 01:49:52,558
(Suddenly feeling confident)

2965
01:49:52,558 --> 01:49:53,828
I can't seem to keep my head up straight.

2966
01:49:54,058 --> 01:49:55,358
I keep doing this.

2967
01:49:55,358 --> 01:49:56,358
(The magical, confidence-boosting jacket)

2968
01:49:57,258 --> 01:49:58,328
It's definitely light.

2969
01:49:58,328 --> 01:50:00,468
So it's easier to dance with the jacket on.

2970
01:50:00,468 --> 01:50:02,768
It's a good jacket to put on while dancing.

2971
01:50:02,768 --> 01:50:04,098
It makes the choreography...

2972
01:50:04,138 --> 01:50:05,538
look cool.

2973
01:50:05,898 --> 01:50:07,338
(Making his choreography hip)

2974
01:50:07,338 --> 01:50:08,768
This definitely makes me look cool.

2975
01:50:08,768 --> 01:50:09,768
Check out the zippers.

2976
01:50:09,768 --> 01:50:11,378
- It's got two zippers.
- Yes.

2977
01:50:11,438 --> 01:50:13,478
You can style the jacket however you want then.

2978
01:50:13,548 --> 01:50:14,648
It looks stylish.

2979
01:50:14,648 --> 01:50:16,848
(Papa Koo is excited now that he looks cool.)

2980
01:50:17,018 --> 01:50:18,018
(Jumping with excitement)

2981
01:50:19,048 --> 01:50:20,318
(Grooving just like Koo Young)

2982
01:50:20,318 --> 01:50:21,588
It's much more stylish.

2983
01:50:21,588 --> 01:50:23,088
It's light and warm. I like it.

2984
01:50:23,088 --> 01:50:24,358
It must be a new version.

2985
01:50:24,358 --> 01:50:25,758
I don't want to take it off.

2986
01:50:25,758 --> 01:50:26,818
(It's right up his alley.)

2987
01:50:26,818 --> 01:50:28,058
- Let's practice with the jacket on.
- Okay.

2988
01:50:28,058 --> 01:50:29,058
Let's do this.

2989
01:50:29,058 --> 01:50:30,398
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2990
01:50:30,398 --> 01:50:31,728
(Fully charged and ready for battle)

2991
01:50:31,898 --> 01:50:33,768
(Back to practicing)

2992
01:50:33,898 --> 01:50:35,598
(His confidence level is maxed out.)

2993
01:50:37,298 --> 01:50:38,768
(Their practice is going smoothly.)

2994
01:50:38,998 --> 01:50:41,068
(The 4-person team is warming up.)

2995
01:50:41,068 --> 01:50:42,368
- Isn't it light?
- Yes.

2996
01:50:42,368 --> 01:50:43,578
I feel light.

2997
01:50:43,578 --> 01:50:44,638
And the jacket feels light too.

2998
01:50:44,638 --> 01:50:45,778
It's a great color too.

2999
01:50:45,838 --> 01:50:47,378
It looks great on me.

3000
01:50:47,378 --> 01:50:48,578
MIN JUN. Look.

3001
01:50:48,578 --> 01:50:50,008
The two-way zipper looks great. Try it.

3002
01:50:50,378 --> 01:50:52,178
- I see. Like this?
- Yes. That's it.

3003
01:50:52,178 --> 01:50:54,088
Like this?

3004
01:50:54,348 --> 01:50:55,888
- Like this?
- Yes. MIN JUN.

3005
01:50:55,948 --> 01:50:57,658
We can style the jacket however we want.

3006
01:50:58,088 --> 01:51:00,058
I can easily practice with the jacket on.

3007
01:51:00,058 --> 01:51:01,458
- I can do this.
- And this too.

3008
01:51:01,528 --> 01:51:03,358
- It looks super hip.
- Exactly.

3009
01:51:03,558 --> 01:51:04,998
(They practice wearing the hip jacket.)

3010
01:51:05,098 --> 01:51:06,658
(Wearing a smile too)

3011
01:51:06,658 --> 01:51:08,128
(Their dancing is full of confidence.)

3012
01:51:08,128 --> 01:51:09,228
Faster!

3013
01:51:09,998 --> 01:51:13,168
(The 4-person team finishes practicing too.)

3014
01:51:13,168 --> 01:51:14,708
(The day of the filming)

3015
01:51:14,708 --> 01:51:16,168
This is crazy, seriously.

3016
01:51:17,008 --> 01:51:18,208
This is crazy.

3017
01:51:18,838 --> 01:51:20,748
You look so cute. Oh, my.

3018
01:51:20,748 --> 01:51:21,848
(Beaming eyes)

3019
01:51:22,048 --> 01:51:23,448
(Ta-da)

3020
01:51:23,448 --> 01:51:24,578
(Their defense is down.)

3021
01:51:24,878 --> 01:51:26,848
- You look so cute.
- So cute.

3022
01:51:26,918 --> 01:51:28,818
We cast the perfect girl for the role.

3023
01:51:28,818 --> 01:51:30,018
Our film is going to rock.

3024
01:51:30,118 --> 01:51:31,418
(They start off with Chapter 1, directed by INGYOO.)

3025
01:51:31,418 --> 01:51:33,018
In this chapter, ShiN exudes...

3026
01:51:33,018 --> 01:51:34,328
this timid vibe.

3027
01:51:34,328 --> 01:51:36,188
She has her role models...

3028
01:51:36,258 --> 01:51:37,928
and wants to be like them.

3029
01:51:37,928 --> 01:51:39,128
It's the start of the story.

3030
01:51:39,328 --> 01:51:40,868
Since not a lot of dancers will be in my chapter,

3031
01:51:40,868 --> 01:51:42,398
I tried to think of many ways...

3032
01:51:42,398 --> 01:51:44,238
to leave a strong impression.

3033
01:51:44,238 --> 01:51:45,438
Do you want to try this instead?

3034
01:51:45,438 --> 01:51:47,038
Do the same steps.

3035
01:51:47,168 --> 01:51:49,338
(The version with regular steps)

3036
01:51:49,338 --> 01:51:51,008
Let's try that while you make a turn.

3037
01:51:51,008 --> 01:51:54,308
(The version with turns)

3038
01:51:54,308 --> 01:51:55,548
Keep it smooth and relaxed.

3039
01:51:55,548 --> 01:51:57,748
(Making it look effortless)

3040
01:51:57,878 --> 01:51:59,218
Perfect.

3041
01:51:59,278 --> 01:52:00,548
Do you not like it?

3042
01:52:00,548 --> 01:52:01,648
Are you not happy with it?

3043
01:52:02,648 --> 01:52:04,318
She's not happy with it. Let's try one more time.

3044
01:52:04,618 --> 01:52:05,758
Quickly.

3045
01:52:05,758 --> 01:52:07,128
Things got seriously delayed.

3046
01:52:07,128 --> 01:52:09,328
It was delayed even from INGYOO's chapter.

3047
01:52:09,388 --> 01:52:10,798
This was the order of our shoot.

3048
01:52:10,798 --> 01:52:12,028
INGYOO's chapter,

3049
01:52:12,028 --> 01:52:13,598
my chapter,

3050
01:52:13,598 --> 01:52:15,498
Simeez's chapter, and MIN JUN's chapter.

3051
01:52:15,528 --> 01:52:17,168
He was supposed to take that long.

3052
01:52:17,268 --> 01:52:18,468
We had to film fast.

3053
01:52:18,738 --> 01:52:21,308
The weather affected my scene the most.

3054
01:52:21,308 --> 01:52:23,778
I was worried that the sun would go down soon.

3055
01:52:23,978 --> 01:52:26,908
There's already an hour and a half delay.

3056
01:52:26,908 --> 01:52:29,748
Despite the delay, INGYOO tried to work on the details.

3057
01:52:30,618 --> 01:52:32,148
Let's play it again, so the kids can watch it.

3058
01:52:32,148 --> 01:52:33,178
(Isn't this great?)

3059
01:52:33,318 --> 01:52:35,318
I didn't want to force the kids.

3060
01:52:35,318 --> 01:52:36,718
That will only make them cry.

3061
01:52:36,718 --> 01:52:38,888
At this rate, we're going to...

3062
01:52:38,888 --> 01:52:40,218
run into a problem.

3063
01:52:40,218 --> 01:52:41,488
I was thinking,

3064
01:52:41,488 --> 01:52:43,028
"Remember that this is an individual match too."

3065
01:52:43,028 --> 01:52:44,158
"This is risky."

3066
01:52:44,158 --> 01:52:45,398
We need to film my chapter first.

3067
01:52:45,398 --> 01:52:47,198
Looking at the weather, it would be dark by the time...

3068
01:52:47,198 --> 01:52:48,698
- BADA finishes hers.
- That makes sense.

3069
01:52:48,798 --> 01:52:50,338
They changed the order.

3070
01:52:50,368 --> 01:52:52,068
There's a two-hour delay.

3071
01:52:52,698 --> 01:52:54,408
I need to film mine quickly then.

3072
01:52:54,708 --> 01:52:56,608
I was a bit embarrassed.

3073
01:52:56,868 --> 01:52:59,478
Please pay attention, so I can only go over this once.

3074
01:52:59,478 --> 01:53:01,208
It was the last chapter of our story.

3075
01:53:01,208 --> 01:53:02,948
It's the closing segment.

3076
01:53:02,948 --> 01:53:04,448
I wanted to do the group dance.

3077
01:53:04,518 --> 01:53:05,648
My gosh. It's hot.

3078
01:53:05,778 --> 01:53:07,248
They're already tired.

3079
01:53:07,248 --> 01:53:08,548
The kids completely lost focus.

3080
01:53:08,648 --> 01:53:10,488
Given the size of the group,

3081
01:53:10,488 --> 01:53:11,688
I needed an assistant...

3082
01:53:11,688 --> 01:53:12,958
to film a dance video.

3083
01:53:12,958 --> 01:53:14,658
Sorry to ask this, INGYOO. Could you go up there...

3084
01:53:15,028 --> 01:53:16,158
and do what I say?

3085
01:53:16,158 --> 01:53:17,728
(INGYOO: Simeez's assistant)

3086
01:53:19,328 --> 01:53:20,698
- Here?
- INGYOO.

3087
01:53:20,698 --> 01:53:22,728
Move the podium, so they can step on it.

3088
01:53:23,568 --> 01:53:24,798
- INGYOO.
- Okay.

3089
01:53:24,798 --> 01:53:25,898
Get on the podium.

3090
01:53:25,898 --> 01:53:26,898
A little more.

3091
01:53:27,538 --> 01:53:28,608
I want Ra On to stand where you are.

3092
01:53:28,608 --> 01:53:29,668
Okay.

3093
01:53:29,738 --> 01:53:30,838
Send Eun Seo there.

3094
01:53:30,838 --> 01:53:32,608
Could you mark their spots with tape?

3095
01:53:32,608 --> 01:53:34,178
INGYOO, help those 30 dancers find their spots.

3096
01:53:34,308 --> 01:53:37,118
Group of 30 dancers. Please come on out.

3097
01:53:37,118 --> 01:53:39,518
INGYOO, can you get them to stand more closely?

3098
01:53:39,518 --> 01:53:41,248
- Stand more closely.
- Okay.

3099
01:53:41,248 --> 01:53:42,318
Hinowa, move half a step.

3100
01:53:42,318 --> 01:53:43,858
(Interpreting)

3101
01:53:44,188 --> 01:53:45,188
That's the spot.

3102
01:53:45,188 --> 01:53:46,218
It's great.

3103
01:53:46,218 --> 01:53:47,958
- Looks great.
- Looks great.

3104
01:53:48,158 --> 01:53:49,888
- We're ready.
- Let's go.

3105
01:53:49,958 --> 01:53:51,528
- Here we go.
- Five...

3106
01:53:52,328 --> 01:53:53,998
(INGYOO is counting down too.)

3107
01:53:56,768 --> 01:53:58,268
She must've felt anxious.

3108
01:53:58,268 --> 01:53:59,368
I thought...

3109
01:53:59,368 --> 01:54:01,768
I should get their energy level up and hype them up.

3110
01:54:04,308 --> 01:54:07,278
(The captain of the cheer squad for Super Kids)

3111
01:54:07,278 --> 01:54:09,708
The kids are struggling in the heat.

3112
01:54:09,708 --> 01:54:11,578
- This is hitting them hard. Yes.
- Are they that exhausted?

3113
01:54:12,178 --> 01:54:13,278
I have no choice, though.

3114
01:54:13,888 --> 01:54:16,218
This is tough. We're colleagues.

3115
01:54:16,388 --> 01:54:17,518
But we're also competitors.

3116
01:54:17,518 --> 01:54:19,358
I'm at a disadvantage because we changed the order.

3117
01:54:19,418 --> 01:54:21,658
I'm very worried about their energy level.

3118
01:54:21,658 --> 01:54:23,128
I was upset.

3119
01:54:23,188 --> 01:54:25,498
(The shoot of the 3-person team)

3120
01:54:25,498 --> 01:54:28,428
(Back Koo Young starts filming first.)

3121
01:54:28,568 --> 01:54:31,438
Not to fall behind the schedule,

3122
01:54:31,568 --> 01:54:34,308
- Seven, eight.
- we had to secure several scenes.

3123
01:54:34,308 --> 01:54:36,738
Yurichika did a great job keeping up with the choreography.

3124
01:54:38,408 --> 01:54:40,138
She's such a good dancer.

3125
01:54:40,908 --> 01:54:42,678
There's no problem with the choreography, right?

3126
01:54:42,748 --> 01:54:43,748
(Nodding)

3127
01:54:44,318 --> 01:54:45,648
Yurichika.

3128
01:54:46,348 --> 01:54:48,048
Are you okay playing the main character?

3129
01:54:48,588 --> 01:54:49,688
I kept speaking Japanese to her.

3130
01:54:49,688 --> 01:54:51,558
I wanted to save time on interpretation.

3131
01:54:51,558 --> 01:54:54,058
I was able to make jokes...

3132
01:54:54,058 --> 01:54:56,388
in Japanese to Japanese kids.

3133
01:54:57,198 --> 01:54:59,958
Should I say I was able to break down the barrier?

3134
01:55:00,428 --> 01:55:02,698
There's so much to convey in Chapter Two.

3135
01:55:02,698 --> 01:55:03,998
I had a secret weapon.

3136
01:55:03,998 --> 01:55:05,168
I was confident.

3137
01:55:06,538 --> 01:55:08,738
I thought Koo Young's story was too difficult to understand...

3138
01:55:09,238 --> 01:55:10,408
and it wasn't audience-friendly.

3139
01:55:10,408 --> 01:55:11,838
She said she didn't know what it was about.

3140
01:55:11,838 --> 01:55:13,778
I think I can do a better job than Koo Young.

3141
01:55:14,848 --> 01:55:17,548
- But why did you mess up?
- Me?

3142
01:55:17,548 --> 01:55:18,778
- Mr. Back Koo Young was too good.
- Right.

3143
01:55:18,778 --> 01:55:20,918
- He was so good.
- This one.

3144
01:55:20,918 --> 01:55:21,918
(They watched Episode 1.)

3145
01:55:21,918 --> 01:55:23,518
By the way,

3146
01:55:23,588 --> 01:55:25,688
- why do you always look down?
- Right.

3147
01:55:26,058 --> 01:55:27,928
(Kasper staring at the floor in Episode 1)

3148
01:55:27,988 --> 01:55:29,488
If you glared like this,

3149
01:55:29,558 --> 01:55:31,258
you could've gotten one more vote.

3150
01:55:31,258 --> 01:55:32,858
Then it might not have been 9 to 0.

3151
01:55:32,858 --> 01:55:34,128
(They're driving me crazy.)

3152
01:55:34,128 --> 01:55:36,468
Chapter Three is about the group dance.

3153
01:55:36,598 --> 01:55:40,238
It's the only chapter with everyone dancing together.

3154
01:55:40,238 --> 01:55:41,708
I wanted to show the audience...

3155
01:55:41,708 --> 01:55:45,408
that even Kids Dancer can pull off an amazing performance like this.

3156
01:55:45,578 --> 01:55:46,678
So...

3157
01:55:46,908 --> 01:55:49,008
It might have been difficult for the kids,

3158
01:55:49,008 --> 01:55:51,148
but we needed to make sure everyone danced in sync.

3159
01:55:51,148 --> 01:55:53,678
Kids, the location of the water bottles has to match.

3160
01:55:57,018 --> 01:55:58,158
Again.

3161
01:55:58,258 --> 01:55:59,718
Seven. Stop.

3162
01:56:00,728 --> 01:56:02,228
Let's try again.

3163
01:56:02,228 --> 01:56:03,528
Seven, eight.

3164
01:56:03,528 --> 01:56:04,698
(Who got it wrong?)

3165
01:56:04,698 --> 01:56:06,028
(You?)

3166
01:56:06,498 --> 01:56:07,498
(Again)

3167
01:56:07,498 --> 01:56:09,228
(Only you guys will try again.)

3168
01:56:09,568 --> 01:56:10,798
(Let's try again.)

3169
01:56:10,798 --> 01:56:13,038
Since they're only kids, he talked to them nicely.

3170
01:56:13,038 --> 01:56:14,968
- "Again."
- But he sounded scarier.

3171
01:56:14,968 --> 01:56:16,038
(Re-do Ghost)

3172
01:56:16,108 --> 01:56:18,138
(They perfectly film the water bottle part.)

3173
01:56:18,138 --> 01:56:19,408
I was very satisfied.

3174
01:56:19,808 --> 01:56:22,108
It was a lot of fun, and we wrapped it up well.

3175
01:56:22,108 --> 01:56:23,108
I wasn't worried.

3176
01:56:23,108 --> 01:56:24,378
I was very confident.

3177
01:56:24,648 --> 01:56:25,818
One, two!

3178
01:56:25,818 --> 01:56:28,718
(Simeez's Chapter 4 shoot enters its final stretch.)

3179
01:56:28,788 --> 01:56:31,788
When shooting Simeez's chapter, I thought there would be light rain.

3180
01:56:31,788 --> 01:56:33,218
(Heavy rain)

3181
01:56:33,218 --> 01:56:34,928
Okay!

3182
01:56:35,458 --> 01:56:37,358
Goodness.

3183
01:56:37,658 --> 01:56:39,198
The children's energy...

3184
01:56:39,198 --> 01:56:40,228
Our part is in trouble.

3185
01:56:40,228 --> 01:56:41,728
They would really want to go home.

3186
01:56:41,728 --> 01:56:43,528
They were all soaked.

3187
01:56:43,528 --> 01:56:46,098
Even their shoes were wet.

3188
01:56:46,498 --> 01:56:48,208
What is he going to do? He's going last.

3189
01:56:48,408 --> 01:56:50,778
I had to work with the children at the end...

3190
01:56:50,778 --> 01:56:51,778
when their energy levels would be the lowest.

3191
01:56:51,778 --> 01:56:55,278
I think I felt sensitive and upset.

3192
01:56:55,508 --> 01:56:57,678
I can see everyone seated.

3193
01:56:57,678 --> 01:56:59,718
Try it. You can do it.

3194
01:56:59,778 --> 01:57:01,948
Five, six, seven, eight, one...

3195
01:57:01,948 --> 01:57:03,688
Chapter Two...

3196
01:57:03,688 --> 01:57:06,088
is about battle, the beginning of the conflict.

3197
01:57:06,088 --> 01:57:09,088
It's the most powerful part of the film.

3198
01:57:09,088 --> 01:57:11,358
I put a lot of effort into every shot...

3199
01:57:11,358 --> 01:57:12,998
so it could convey energetic...

3200
01:57:12,998 --> 01:57:16,028
and powerful moves.

3201
01:57:16,198 --> 01:57:19,668
I also want my part to be the kick of the film.

3202
01:57:20,438 --> 01:57:21,738
You can tell from the children's faces.

3203
01:57:21,738 --> 01:57:23,208
They were totally dazed.

3204
01:57:23,208 --> 01:57:27,308
I wasn't sure if their energy levels could handle it.

3205
01:57:27,448 --> 01:57:29,208
I was very anxious.

3206
01:57:29,208 --> 01:57:31,378
I really don't want to go to the Last Stage.

3207
01:57:31,518 --> 01:57:33,418
That could be my driving force.

3208
01:57:33,418 --> 01:57:35,518
But it feels devastating and disappointing.

3209
01:57:35,918 --> 01:57:36,988
It's tough.

3210
01:57:37,148 --> 01:57:39,088
My strength...

3211
01:57:39,088 --> 01:57:40,218
is my uniqueness.

3212
01:57:40,218 --> 01:57:42,128
The new paradigm I want to introduce...

3213
01:57:42,128 --> 01:57:44,198
uses cinematic directing techniques.

3214
01:57:44,598 --> 01:57:46,628
The main character is in panic because the mask fell off,

3215
01:57:46,628 --> 01:57:47,768
and his breath needs to stop.

3216
01:57:48,098 --> 01:57:50,868
I want that to be delivered to the audience as well.

3217
01:57:51,698 --> 01:57:55,168
I could tell from their faces that we couldn't go on like that.

3218
01:57:55,268 --> 01:57:59,308
So I tried to move on as long as I was okay with the takes.

3219
01:58:00,508 --> 01:58:02,608
Well done!

3220
01:58:03,478 --> 01:58:05,178
Good job!

3221
01:58:05,918 --> 01:58:07,688
(NOL Festival: A chance to see the Top 4 perform and teach classes)

3222
01:58:07,688 --> 01:58:09,088
(For more details, please check the NOL app.)

3223
01:58:09,218 --> 01:58:11,558
Is it already 1pm? Time is flying.

3224
01:58:11,958 --> 01:58:13,218
Back Koo Young.

3225
01:58:13,218 --> 01:58:14,288
What's that?

3226
01:58:14,288 --> 01:58:16,328
- BABYZOO.
- What is that?

3227
01:58:16,728 --> 01:58:18,528
(A special message that crossed borders)

3228
01:58:18,698 --> 01:58:21,098
How cute.

3229
01:58:21,098 --> 01:58:22,468
Hello. I'm Niuniu.

3230
01:58:22,468 --> 01:58:24,238
I got back home safely.

3231
01:58:25,068 --> 01:58:27,568
Thank you for creating...

3232
01:58:27,568 --> 01:58:29,368
such an amazing choreography...

3233
01:58:29,368 --> 01:58:30,938
that brought out our strengths.

3234
01:58:30,938 --> 01:58:32,038
I think...

3235
01:58:32,038 --> 01:58:33,708
you're very cool...

3236
01:58:33,708 --> 01:58:35,248
and charismatic when you dance.

3237
01:58:35,248 --> 01:58:37,748
I've improved so much thanks to your classes.

3238
01:58:38,678 --> 01:58:41,788
Thank you for putting so much thought...

3239
01:58:41,788 --> 01:58:43,218
into the choreography for the main character.

3240
01:58:43,218 --> 01:58:44,718
I really enjoyed...

3241
01:58:44,718 --> 01:58:46,618
getting to talk with you...

3242
01:58:46,618 --> 01:58:48,088
on the last day of filming.

3243
01:58:48,158 --> 01:58:49,328
(A proud dad smile)

3244
01:58:49,328 --> 01:58:52,358
You brought us so much joy...

3245
01:58:52,358 --> 01:58:54,898
with your unique choreography and classes.

3246
01:58:55,528 --> 01:58:58,938
Thank you for complimenting my waacking.

3247
01:58:58,938 --> 01:59:00,538
Would you like to do it alone, Rikka?

3248
01:59:00,538 --> 01:59:01,668
Seven, eight!

3249
01:59:01,668 --> 01:59:03,568
(No problem)

3250
01:59:04,078 --> 01:59:06,238
I'll work hard to get even better.

3251
01:59:06,238 --> 01:59:09,578
I didn't know who Kasper was at first.

3252
01:59:09,578 --> 01:59:11,348
So I looked up the preview.

3253
01:59:11,348 --> 01:59:12,378
You were scary.

3254
01:59:12,378 --> 01:59:13,448
(Laughing)

3255
01:59:13,578 --> 01:59:15,288
- Did you see me?
- Yes.

3256
01:59:15,288 --> 01:59:17,088
Was I very scary?

3257
01:59:17,088 --> 01:59:18,188
Yes.

3258
01:59:18,618 --> 01:59:21,088
I went there feeling really nervous.

3259
01:59:21,088 --> 01:59:23,928
But you were very nice and fun.

3260
01:59:24,028 --> 01:59:25,558
(Kasper's talent show)

3261
01:59:25,698 --> 01:59:26,998
Thank you...

3262
01:59:26,998 --> 01:59:29,698
for playing with us even during break time.

3263
01:59:29,728 --> 01:59:32,638
Who told you to cheat at such a young age?

3264
01:59:35,308 --> 01:59:37,408
(A surprise birthday party for Honatsu)

3265
01:59:37,408 --> 01:59:38,778
(Happy...)

3266
01:59:38,778 --> 01:59:40,208
(birthday)

3267
01:59:40,208 --> 01:59:42,578
I was very surprised...

3268
01:59:42,578 --> 01:59:43,878
when you wished me a happy birthday.

3269
01:59:43,878 --> 01:59:47,048
I still have the squishy and treasure it.

3270
01:59:47,148 --> 01:59:49,988
- Thank you, Kasper!
- Thank you, Kasper!

3271
01:59:50,888 --> 01:59:52,858
The experiences I had...

3272
01:59:52,858 --> 01:59:54,258
in Korea...

3273
01:59:54,258 --> 01:59:55,988
were all new,

3274
01:59:55,988 --> 01:59:58,828
but I enjoyed it because I made lots of new friends.

3275
02:00:00,128 --> 02:00:02,398
I want to dance together...

3276
02:00:02,398 --> 02:00:06,268
and be on stage with the teachers.

3277
02:00:06,268 --> 02:00:08,368
I'll work hard...

3278
02:00:08,368 --> 02:00:11,138
to become a better dancer...

3279
02:00:11,138 --> 02:00:12,808
so I can dance with you someday.

3280
02:00:12,808 --> 02:00:16,448
Thank you for teaching me.

3281
02:00:16,648 --> 02:00:18,418
Thank you so much.

3282
02:00:18,418 --> 02:00:19,678
Thank you!

3283
02:00:19,678 --> 02:00:20,678
How cute.

3284
02:00:21,788 --> 02:00:23,248
Bye. See you again.

3285
02:00:23,248 --> 02:00:24,988
I love you. Thank you.

3286
02:00:24,988 --> 02:00:27,118
See you again.

3287
02:00:28,628 --> 02:00:30,488
How cute.

3288
02:00:30,488 --> 02:00:33,028
(Cute...)

3289
02:00:35,668 --> 02:00:37,698
They all got home safely.

3290
02:00:37,798 --> 02:00:39,398
They really worked hard.

3291
02:00:39,398 --> 02:00:40,808
I'm really...

3292
02:00:40,808 --> 02:00:41,968
grateful.

3293
02:00:41,968 --> 02:00:44,608
I still have this on my wallpaper.

3294
02:00:44,608 --> 02:00:46,978
It's a picture I took myself.

3295
02:00:46,978 --> 02:00:50,378
I feel really bad that I couldn't buy Honatsu soy-marinated crab.

3296
02:00:50,378 --> 02:00:52,248
He really wanted to try it.

3297
02:00:52,818 --> 02:00:54,848
I want to try soy-marinated crab.

3298
02:00:56,048 --> 02:00:57,618
He's asking you to buy him soy-marinated crab.

3299
02:00:57,618 --> 02:00:59,418
Okay.

3300
02:00:59,518 --> 02:01:02,258
I'm definitely going to buy soy-marinated crab for Honatsu.

3301
02:01:02,758 --> 02:01:05,398
Hi, I'm Kasper.

3302
02:01:05,398 --> 02:01:08,228
I feel awkward filming such a message.

3303
02:01:08,228 --> 02:01:09,998
I really loved...

3304
02:01:09,998 --> 02:01:12,198
spending time with you all.

3305
02:01:12,198 --> 02:01:15,638
There were many scenes I had only imagined.

3306
02:01:15,638 --> 02:01:17,608
But I was able to make them come true...

3307
02:01:17,608 --> 02:01:19,478
thanks to the Kids Dancers.

3308
02:01:19,478 --> 02:01:21,348
So I want to thank you once again,

3309
02:01:21,348 --> 02:01:23,008
and say you really worked hard.

3310
02:01:23,008 --> 02:01:25,448
I hope this film will be something you're proud of...

3311
02:01:25,448 --> 02:01:27,988
when you see it later.

3312
02:01:27,988 --> 02:01:30,958
I'm not sure if we'll be able to meet when you're older,

3313
02:01:30,958 --> 02:01:34,018
but I hope we can work on another great project together someday.

3314
02:01:34,018 --> 02:01:35,588
Don't get sick, eat well,

3315
02:01:35,588 --> 02:01:36,658
study hard,

3316
02:01:36,658 --> 02:01:37,728
and listen to your parents.

3317
02:01:37,728 --> 02:01:38,928
I miss you.

3318
02:01:38,928 --> 02:01:39,928
I love you.

3319
02:01:40,158 --> 02:01:41,268
BADA.

3320
02:01:41,698 --> 02:01:43,868
(The kids' heartfelt messages reach the 4-member team as well.)

3321
02:01:43,868 --> 02:01:44,868
(Smiling automatically)

3322
02:01:44,938 --> 02:01:46,568
(What is this?)

3323
02:01:46,738 --> 02:01:48,408
I got home safely!

3324
02:01:48,408 --> 02:01:51,108
Hello! I got back to Japan safely!

3325
02:01:51,108 --> 02:01:52,438
(He's cute.)

3326
02:01:52,608 --> 02:01:54,278
They filmed this at home?

3327
02:01:54,378 --> 02:01:58,878
Thank you for taking such good care of us and teaching us.

3328
02:01:58,878 --> 02:02:01,718
You're a really cute person.

3329
02:02:01,718 --> 02:02:03,718
You're like a Barbie doll in a movie.

3330
02:02:03,848 --> 02:02:04,918
(She's touched.)

3331
02:02:04,918 --> 02:02:07,258
You taught us house dance in our first class.

3332
02:02:07,258 --> 02:02:09,528
I wasn't familiar with the house style before,

3333
02:02:09,528 --> 02:02:11,698
but you really taught us well.

3334
02:02:11,698 --> 02:02:14,398
It was difficult because it was a new genre,

3335
02:02:14,398 --> 02:02:17,568
but you taught us everything patiently and kindly.

3336
02:02:17,568 --> 02:02:19,868
Thank you so much.

3337
02:02:20,038 --> 02:02:22,638
You're a very stylish person.

3338
02:02:22,638 --> 02:02:24,608
I think your choreography is really cool.

3339
02:02:24,638 --> 02:02:26,738
You're good-looking.

3340
02:02:26,738 --> 02:02:27,948
(Me?)

3341
02:02:28,478 --> 02:02:31,148
Our freestyle was really in sync.

3342
02:02:31,148 --> 02:02:32,748
I had so much fun.

3343
02:02:33,718 --> 02:02:35,048
I was able to enjoy freestyle dance...

3344
02:02:35,048 --> 02:02:38,058
thanks to you.

3345
02:02:38,058 --> 02:02:39,688
One, two, three, four.

3346
02:02:39,688 --> 02:02:40,688
Nice!

3347
02:02:41,328 --> 02:02:42,388
(That's right!)

3348
02:02:42,558 --> 02:02:44,628
(Smiling)

3349
02:02:45,658 --> 02:02:48,568
You played with me in the practice room every day.

3350
02:02:48,568 --> 02:02:50,328
I had so much fun.

3351
02:02:50,698 --> 02:02:53,798
(JEONG MIN JUN)

3352
02:02:53,838 --> 02:02:56,768
Your humorous teaching style...

3353
02:02:56,768 --> 02:02:59,078
kept us laughing throughout the practices,

3354
02:02:59,078 --> 02:03:01,848
and we were able to finish the project while having fun.

3355
02:03:03,508 --> 02:03:06,748
I really love your dance.

3356
02:03:06,748 --> 02:03:08,718
She's wearing glasses.

3357
02:03:08,718 --> 02:03:11,688
You're especially great at dancing.

3358
02:03:11,688 --> 02:03:13,818
You're really cool.

3359
02:03:13,818 --> 02:03:16,828
Your choreography...

3360
02:03:16,828 --> 02:03:18,528
helped me discover...

3361
02:03:18,528 --> 02:03:19,758
a different side of myself.

3362
02:03:19,958 --> 02:03:21,998
One, two, three!

3363
02:03:21,998 --> 02:03:24,368
Thank you for helping me...

3364
02:03:24,368 --> 02:03:28,308
practice each part...

3365
02:03:28,308 --> 02:03:31,608
until I could do it right.

3366
02:03:31,608 --> 02:03:35,578
I remember you getting us a bundle of snacks.

3367
02:03:35,578 --> 02:03:37,718
I was really happy.

3368
02:03:37,718 --> 02:03:40,378
And bacon potato.

3369
02:03:40,378 --> 02:03:41,818
Okay.

3370
02:03:41,818 --> 02:03:43,448
(I guess snacks really are the best.)

3371
02:03:43,648 --> 02:03:45,688
I'm so happy...

3372
02:03:45,688 --> 02:03:49,158
I got to take part in Super Kids Direct Mission...

3373
02:03:49,158 --> 02:03:51,228
and create something together with all of you.

3374
02:03:51,228 --> 02:03:53,328
I had so much fun,

3375
02:03:53,328 --> 02:03:55,328
and it was an experience unlike anything I'd had before.

3376
02:03:55,328 --> 02:03:57,868
It was really nice.

3377
02:03:57,868 --> 02:04:00,268
Thank you for the letter you wrote me.

3378
02:04:00,268 --> 02:04:03,238
I wanted to give the children a cute memory,

3379
02:04:03,238 --> 02:04:05,608
so I bought some four-leaf clover keychains.

3380
02:04:05,608 --> 02:04:08,908
Each leaf represents the four of us.

3381
02:04:09,048 --> 02:04:12,348
I'll always carry this keychain as a symbol of good luck.

3382
02:04:12,348 --> 02:04:15,348
They're so cute.

3383
02:04:15,348 --> 02:04:18,188
I really want to dance with you again.

3384
02:04:18,188 --> 02:04:20,118
Let's make sure to meet again.

3385
02:04:20,118 --> 02:04:23,328
I want to thank you once again.

3386
02:04:23,328 --> 02:04:25,628
Thank you for teaching me.

3387
02:04:25,628 --> 02:04:27,398
I hope to see you again.

3388
02:04:27,768 --> 02:04:28,928
Thank you.

3389
02:04:28,928 --> 02:04:30,028
I love you.

3390
02:04:30,028 --> 02:04:31,268
Bye.

3391
02:04:33,568 --> 02:04:34,568
They're cute.

3392
02:04:34,568 --> 02:04:35,768
How cute.

3393
02:04:35,768 --> 02:04:37,238
This is what it feels like.

3394
02:04:37,238 --> 02:04:39,408
It's like the kids I taught in kindergarten...

3395
02:04:39,408 --> 02:04:41,278
just graduated.

3396
02:04:41,278 --> 02:04:43,448
This is so nice. My heart feels warm.

3397
02:04:43,448 --> 02:04:46,578
I found an oasis...

3398
02:04:46,578 --> 02:04:47,888
in this dry, desert-like place.

3399
02:04:47,888 --> 02:04:49,318
This reminded me...

3400
02:04:49,318 --> 02:04:51,558
what it means to be a teacher again.

3401
02:04:51,558 --> 02:04:52,788
As a teacher...

3402
02:04:52,788 --> 02:04:55,758
They worked so hard and I'm so grateful.

3403
02:04:55,758 --> 02:04:57,488
So no matter how this ends,

3404
02:04:57,488 --> 02:05:00,258
I hope they don't get shaken...

3405
02:05:00,258 --> 02:05:02,168
by the strength of the time we spent together.

3406
02:05:03,698 --> 02:05:06,368
Hello.

3407
02:05:06,398 --> 02:05:08,508
This cold atmosphere.

3408
02:05:08,508 --> 02:05:09,868
The results day.

3409
02:05:10,608 --> 02:05:13,208
(Sighing)

3410
02:05:13,308 --> 02:05:15,708
Today is the day the results are announced.

3411
02:05:16,078 --> 02:05:17,648
My hands keep sweating.

3412
02:05:17,778 --> 02:05:20,948
We can watch the other team's final version.

3413
02:05:20,948 --> 02:05:22,748
I was curious to see...

3414
02:05:22,748 --> 02:05:24,718
what they did.

3415
02:05:24,718 --> 02:05:25,988
It's hard to predict.

3416
02:05:25,988 --> 02:05:29,158
But Koo Young would have added his storytelling punch.

3417
02:05:29,158 --> 02:05:30,728
